:00:13 (13)\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_60 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0/formal/last_run-99570.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-001-r3s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-99570/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 3}\n11:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Explicit memory byte-lane selection\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The MEM stage currently extracts subword loads with a variable 32-bit right\\nshift and generates store masks with another variable shift. On a small FPGA,\\nthese expressions can infer wider mux networks than the four fixed byte lanes\\nrequire, adding LUT depth and routing to the dmem-to-MEM/WB timing path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The MEM stage currently extracts subword loads with a variable 32-bit right\\nshift and generates store masks with another variable shift. On a small FPGA,\\nthese expressions can infer wider mux networks than the four fixed byte lanes\\nrequire, adding LUT depth and routing to the dmem-to-MEM/WB timing path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the variable shifts with explicit address-lane case selection: a\\nfour-way 8-bit mux for byte loads, a two-way 16-bit mux for aligned halfword\\nloads, and directly decoded constant write masks. This preserves pipeline\\nlatency and all RVFI memory semantics while reducing the width and depth of\\nthe lane-selection logic. Because it does not forward raw dmem data into EX,\\nit avoids the long dmem-to-ALU path that regressed the prior load bypass.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace dynamic subword extraction and byte-mask shifts with explicit fixed-lane muxes and constant mask decoding while preserving alignment traps, sign extension, and RVFI data reporting.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_mem_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed byte and halfword load/store lane tests covering every legal offset, signed and unsigned extension, masks, and misalignment suppression.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace dynamic subword extraction and byte-mask shifts with explicit fixed-lane muxes and constant mask decoding while preserving alignment traps, sign extension, and RVFI data reporting.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_mem_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed byte and halfword load/store lane tests covering every legal offset, signed and unsigned extension, masks, and misalignment suppression.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 431.88, \"delta_pct\": 6.22, \"vs_baseline\": 52.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 183.39, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10435, \"ff\": 2037, \"seeds\": [184.03, 159.87, 183.39], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:07:45.613751Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r4s0 (improvement, +6.22%): Replacing variable subword shifts with explicit byte/halfword lane muxes and constant store-mask decoding reduces FPGA LUT depth on the dmem-to-MEM/WB path while preserving load latency and RVFI memory semantics.\"}\n14:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Reset-valid mask for RAM-inferred register file\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The register file synchronously clears all 1,024 data bits, which forces the\\n32-by-32 array into resettable flops and distributes reset across a large,\\nrouting-heavy structure. The current core is above its LUT target and its\\nfitness is sensitive to routed Fmax, while architectural software only needs\\nunwritten registers to read as zero after reset, not every data bit physically\\ncleared.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The register file synchronously clears all 1,024 data bits, which forces the\\n32-by-32 array into resettable flops and distributes reset across a large,\\nrouting-heavy structure. The current core is above its LUT target and its\\nfitness is sensitive to routed Fmax, while architectural software only needs\\nunwritten registers to read as zero after reset, not every data bit physically\\ncleared.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove reset from the register-data array and add a 32-bit written-valid mask\\nthat is cleared on reset and set on each nonzero register write. Reads return\\nzero when the addressed valid bit is clear, otherwise they return the stored\\ndata; x0 and the existing same-cycle write-first bypass remain unchanged.\\nThis preserves the core's deterministic post-reset behavior and all RVFI\\nregister semantics while making the two-read-port data array eligible for\\ncompact replicated distributed-RAM inference. Replacing roughly 1,024\\nresettable data flops and their reset routing with 32 valid flops plus shallow\\nread gating should reduce placement pressure and improve median Fmax without\\nchanging CoreMark cycles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace full-array reset with a resettable per-register valid mask, leave data storage unreset for distributed-RAM inference, and preserve x0 and write-first read behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_reg_file.py\", \"description\": \"Extend reset tests to write registers, reset again, and verify that the valid mask restores zero-visible state while subsequent writes and same-cycle bypass still work.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace full-array reset with a resettable per-register valid mask, leave data storage unreset for distributed-RAM inference, and preserve x0 and write-first read behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_reg_file.py\", \"description\": \"Extend reset tests to write registers, reset again, and verify that the valid mask restores zero-visible state while subsequent writes and same-cycle bypass still work.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 333.79, \"delta_pct\": -22.71, \"vs_baseline\": 18.02, \"fmax_mhz\": 141.74, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7964, \"ff\": 1249, \"seeds\": [135.34, 145.52, 141.74], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:29:11.095777Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r5s0 (regression, -22.71%): Replacing register-file data reset with an address-indexed valid mask adds a valid-bit lookup and zero-select mux to both asynchronous read paths, so reset-routing savings do not pay when register-read timing is the stronger FPGA constraint.\"}\n17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Share one explicit barrel shifter across SLL, SRL, and SRA\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently expresses left-logical, right-logical, and right-arithmetic\\nshifts as three separate variable-shift operations. On a LUT FPGA these may\\nbecome parallel barrel-shifter networks even though only one ALU operation\\nis selected, consuming LUTs and routing in the execute datapath. The earlier\\nmultiplier-sharing win and fixed memory-lane win show that making mutually\\nexclusive wide operators explicit can materially improve routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently expresses left-logical, right-logical, and right-arithmetic\\nshifts as three separate variable-shift operations. On a LUT FPGA these may\\nbecome parallel barrel-shifter networks even though only one ALU operation\\nis selected, consuming LUTs and routing in the execute datapath. The earlier\\nmultiplier-sharing win and fixed memory-lane win show that making mutually\\nexclusive wide operators explicit can materially improve routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three variable-shift expressions with one explicit five-level\\nright-shift mux network controlled by shamt[4:0]. SLL uses bit-reversed input\\nand bit-reversed output, which turns a left shift into a logical right shift\\nusing only rewiring; SRL uses the network directly with zero fill; SRA uses\\nthe same network with a replicated original sign bit at each enabled level.\\nThis should force sharing of the 32-bit barrel hardware, reduce duplicated\\nLUT and routing pressure, and preserve the current single-cycle latency,\\nCoreMark cycle count, decoder behavior, forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one explicit five-level configurable-fill right barrel shifter, map SLL through static bit reversal, and route SRL/SRA through the same network without changing any other ALU or ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend directed and randomized SLL, SRL, and SRA vectors across all 32 shift amounts, sign-bit cases, and ignored upper bits of the shift operand.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement one explicit five-level configurable-fill right barrel shifter, map SLL through static bit reversal, and route SRL/SRA through the same network without changing any other ALU or ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend directed and randomized SLL, SRL, and SRA vectors across all 32 shift amounts, sign-bit cases, and ignored upper bits of the shift operand.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 398.81, \"delta_pct\": -7.66, \"vs_baseline\": 41.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 169.35, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10182, \"ff\": 2017, \"seeds\": [172.65, 144.2, 169.35], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T16:42:26.038212Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r6s0 (regression, -7.66%): Manually sharing SLL/SRL/SRA as a five-level right-shift mux chain with op-dependent bit reversal and fill can constrain synthesis into extra selection and routing that is slower than native variable-shift inference, so explicit operator sharing must be validated against the FPGA mapper's existing optimization.\"}\n20:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Canonicalize unused source operands before hazard detection\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares a pending load destination with both raw\\nsource bitfields of the following instruction, even when an opcode does not\\narchitecturally read one or either field. Those false matches inject bubbles\\nin immediate arithmetic, loads, jumps, and upper-immediate instructions.\\nAn earlier attempt merely gated the interlock and failed the RVFI register\\ncheck because unused raw source addresses and stale values still propagated\\nto retirement; the optimization must canonicalize the full source contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use interlock compares a pending load destination with both raw\\nsource bitfields of the following instruction, even when an opcode does not\\narchitecturally read one or either field. Those false matches inject bubbles\\nin immediate arithmetic, loads, jumps, and upper-immediate instructions.\\nAn earlier attempt merely gated the interlock and failed the RVFI register\\ncheck because unused raw source addresses and stale values still propagated\\nto retirement; the optimization must canonicalize the full source contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Have the validated decoder identify whether each instruction actually uses\\nrs1 and rs2, then present x0 as the address and zero as the value for every\\nunused source before the ID/EX register. Feed these canonical source addresses\\nto the existing load-use equality checks instead of raw instruction fields.\\nTrue dependencies retain the same one-cycle interlock, while false matches\\ndisappear and unused RVFI source fields remain self-consistent with x0.\\n\\nThis should reduce CoreMark cycles without adding qualifier gates after the\\nhazard comparators or changing forwarding, pipeline latency, bus behavior,\\nretirement, illegal-instruction trapping, or the nret=1 interface. Source-use\\nbits must default false and only assert within validated decoder arms so the\\ndefault-illegal discipline remains intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 controls for each legal RV32IM instruction class, defaulting both false for illegal and source-free instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Canonicalize unused register addresses and values to x0/zero before register-file reads and ID/EX capture so execution and RVFI observe the same source contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive load-use detection from the ID stage's canonical source addresses rather than raw IF instruction bitfields, preserving replay and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename and document the source inputs as canonical architectural addresses while retaining the existing shallow equality-based load-use logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Check true dependencies, false matches in unused fields, canonical RVFI source fields, illegal encodings, replay, and coincident instruction/data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 controls for each legal RV32IM instruction class, defaulting both false for illegal and source-free instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Canonicalize unused register addresses and values to x0/zero before register-file reads and ID/EX capture so execution and RVFI observe the same source contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive load-use detection from the ID stage's canonical source addresses rather than raw IF instruction bitfields, preserving replay and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename and document the source inputs as canonical architectural addresses while retaining the existing shallow equality-based load-use logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Check true dependencies, false matches in unused fields, canonical RVFI source fields, illegal encodings, replay, and coincident instruction/data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 7}\n23:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Target-only replay-buffer tag\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry replay buffer is the only control-flow optimization\\nthat has improved the current core, but each hit compares both the owning\\nbranch PC and the cached target PC. The payload is simply the instruction at\\nthat target, so the branch-PC identity is redundant: any legal, aligned,\\ntaken backward branch resolving to the same target can safely reuse it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry replay buffer is the only control-flow optimization\\nthat has improved the current core, but each hit compares both the owning\\nbranch PC and the cached target PC. The payload is simply the instruction at\\nthat target, so the branch-PC identity is redundant: any legal, aligned,\\ntaken backward branch resolving to the same target can safely reuse it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the stored branch-PC tag, its pending-fill copy, and the parallel\\n32-bit branch-PC equality from the replay-buffer hit path. Retain the exact\\n32-bit target comparison, captured target instruction, confirmed-EX lookup,\\naccepted-fetch fill protocol, and target-plus-four resume behavior unchanged.\\nThis is a strict hardware reduction with no new muxes or qualifiers, and\\nshould reduce comparator fabric, flops, and routing on the replay decision\\nwhile modestly broadening reuse when multiple backward branches share a loop\\nhead. Architectural execution, stalls, RVFI, traps, and nret remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the entry and pending branch-PC tags and qualify confirmed replay hits solely with the existing exact target-PC tag and eligibility signals, preserving fill and replay timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused resolved branch-PC output while retaining legal aligned taken-backward qualification and the exact resolved target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant resolved-branch-PC wiring and update the replay-buffer connection without changing pipeline, bus-stall, or nret=1 behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that same-target backward branches reuse one cached instruction, different targets miss and refill, and replay remains single-shot and stall-safe.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the entry and pending branch-PC tags and qualify confirmed replay hits solely with the existing exact target-PC tag and eligibility signals, preserving fill and replay timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused resolved branch-PC output while retaining legal aligned taken-backward qualification and the exact resolved target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant resolved-branch-PC wiring and update the replay-buffer connection without changing pipeline, bus-stall, or nret=1 behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that same-target backward branches reuse one cached instruction, different targets miss and refill, and replay remains single-shot and stall-safe.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 463.86, \"delta_pct\": 7.4, \"vs_baseline\": 64.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 196.97, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10217, \"ff\": 1956, \"seeds\": [186.25, 197.01, 196.97], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:40:47.746851Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r8s0 (improvement, +7.40%): A confirmed backward-branch replay entry is safely keyed by its exact target alone, so dropping the redundant branch-PC tag removes 32-bit comparator, flop, and routing cost while allowing branches that share a loop head to reuse the cached instruction.\"}\n26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Prune post-execute pipeline payloads\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Introduce stage-specific compact control payloads and remove resolved-branch\\nmetadata after it has produced pc_next and the replay-buffer signals in EX.\\nEX/MEM will retain only memory, writeback, and trap controls; MEM/WB will retain\\nonly register-write, result-select, and trap controls. This is an end-to-end\\ndeletion of unused state with no new mux, comparator, interlock, or fetch-PC\\nfeedback and no change to instruction timing, CoreMark cycles, RVFI fields,\\nbus-stall behavior, or nret. Reducing pipeline-register width and control fanout\\nshould improve placement and routed Fmax while also lowering FF and LUT use.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 436.99, \"delta_pct\": -5.79, \"vs_baseline\": 54.51, \"fmax_mhz\": 185.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10185, \"ff\": 1971, \"seeds\": [179.92, 185.56, 198.93], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:52:35.726601Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
