testbench.register_index (rvfi_reg_check.sv:20.23-20.37): 23\\nSBY 11:52:45 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:04  Assert failed in rvfi_testbench: rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 (_witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56)\\nSBY 11:52:45 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:04  Writing trace to VCD file: engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:04  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:04  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:04  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:05  Status: failed\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:06 (66)\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:41 (41)\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\nSBY 11:52:46 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r6s1/formal/last_run-15381.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r6s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-15381/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): Falling-edge register-file writeback is half a cycle too late for an ID instruction that captures operands on the same rising edge its producer reaches MEM/WB, so removing the WB-to-ID write-first bypass requires an interlock or an earlier architectural write point.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Prune post-execute pipeline payloads\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Introduce stage-specific compact control payloads and remove resolved-branch\\nmetadata after it has produced pc_next and the replay-buffer signals in EX.\\nEX/MEM will retain only memory, writeback, and trap controls; MEM/WB will retain\\nonly register-write, result-select, and trap controls. This is an end-to-end\\ndeletion of unused state with no new mux, comparator, interlock, or fetch-PC\\nfeedback and no change to instruction timing, CoreMark cycles, RVFI fields,\\nbus-stall behavior, or nret. Reducing pipeline-register width and control fanout\\nshould improve placement and routed Fmax while also lowering FF and LUT use.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 436.99, \"delta_pct\": -5.79, \"vs_baseline\": 54.51, \"fmax_mhz\": 185.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10185, \"ff\": 1971, \"seeds\": [179.92, 185.56, 198.93], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:52:35.726601Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9}\neval_result.schema.json\nhypothesis.schema.json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
