{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, yaml\nfrom jsonschema import validate\np = Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml')\ndata = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nschema = json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())\nvalidate(data, schema)\nassert data['id'] == 'hyp-20260711-001-r10s0'\nassert data['category'] == 'micro_opt'\nassert all(x['file'].startswith('rtl/') or x['file'].startswith('test/test_') for x in data['changes'])\nprint(f'valid: {p}')\nprint(f\\\"changes: {len(data['changes'])}; expected delta: {data['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']}%\\\")\nPY\nsed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, yaml\nfrom jsonschema import validate\np = Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml')\ndata = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nschema = json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())\nvalidate(data, schema)\nassert data['id'] == 'hyp-20260711-001-r10s0'\nassert data['category'] == 'micro_opt'\nassert all(x['file'].startswith('rtl/') or x['file'].startswith('test/test_') for x in data['changes'])\nprint(f'valid: {p}')\nprint(f\\\"changes: {len(data['changes'])}; expected delta: {data['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']}%\\\")\nPY\nsed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml\nchanges: 4; expected delta: 3%\nid: hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Valid-only reset for pipeline payload banks\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  ID/EX, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB synchronously clear every bit of their wide packed\n  payloads even though invalid entries are architecturally ignored. This puts\n  reset and flush selection on hundreds of PC, instruction, operand, result,\n  and RVFI-data flops, increasing global control fanout and placement pressure\n  in a design whose fitness is now dominated by routed Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split each pipeline register into a small validity/control bank and a wide\n  data bank. Reset and bubble flushes clear only valid plus the control bits\n  needed to suppress register writes, memory requests, forwarding, and traps;\n  data fields retain or capture don't-care values while invalid and never\n  acquire a reset/flush mux. Keep the existing stall and MEM/WB held-forwarding\n  behavior exactly intact. Unlike the failed register-file valid-mask attempt,\n  this adds no lookup or select to an active operand path: validity already\n  qualifies retirement and side effects. Removing reset/flush fanout from the\n  wide payload flops should improve placement and median Fmax without changing\n  CoreMark cycles, pipeline latency, bus handshakes, RVFI semantics, or nret.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refactor ID/EX into separately clocked control-valid and data banks so reset and flush invalidate the entry without clearing PC, instruction, immediate, register tags, or operand payloads; preserve replay and stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refactor EX/MEM so reset clears valid and side-effect controls only, while the wide execute and RVFI payload bank has no reset mux and continues to hold on data-memory stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refactor MEM/WB into valid, control, and payload banks, retaining the existing hold behavior needed for forwarding while removing reset from wide result, memory, instruction, PC, and operand fields.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline_reset.py\n    description: \"Add directed reset, redirect-flush, load-use bubble, replay, and data-stall checks proving invalid payload values cannot retire, write registers, issue memory requests, perturb forwarding, or violate RVFI once a valid instruction arrives.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
