{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'fill_pending|fill target|pending.*target|entry.*invalidate|replay.*fill' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | head -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decouple fetch with a two-entry instruction FIFO\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current frontend ties the fetch PC directly to backend stalls. Whenever a\\ndata-memory operation freezes EX/MEM, an otherwise-ready instruction-memory\\ncycle is discarded; later random instruction-memory backpressure then creates\\nanother bubble. A shallow fetch queue can use those idle frontend cycles to\\nbuild slack without adding a cache or changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current frontend ties the fetch PC directly to backend stalls. Whenever a\\ndata-memory operation freezes EX/MEM, an otherwise-ready instruction-memory\\ncycle is discarded; later random instruction-memory backpressure then creates\\nanother bubble. A shallow fetch queue can use those idle frontend cycles to\\nbuild slack without adding a cache or changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the tightly coupled IF path with a two-entry fall-through instruction\\nFIFO carrying PC and instruction, and give fetch its own request PC. Enqueue\\nonly when io_imemReady is asserted, dequeue only when ID can advance, and keep\\nfetching during backend and load-use stalls while space remains. On an EX\\nredirect, invalidate all queued wrong-path entries and restart the request PC\\nat the redirect target. Hazard control should stall decode on FIFO-empty rather\\nthan directly on io_imemReady. This should overlap independent iStall and\\ndStall intervals, improving CoreMark iterations/cycle with only a small bank of\\nflops and shallow control muxes, so median Fmax should remain nearly unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the two-entry PC/instruction FIFO, independent fetch request PC, ready-qualified enqueue, decode-qualified dequeue, and redirect flush/restart behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire io_imemReady into the decoupled frontend and connect FIFO-valid/consume control between fetch, hazard control, and ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace direct instruction-bus backpressure handling with frontend-empty and dequeue control while allowing fetch to run during backend stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_fetch_fifo.py\", \"description\": \"Add cocotb checks for ready-qualified fetches, prefetch during backend stalls, FIFO-empty bubbles, in-order delivery, and complete wrong-path invalidation on redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the two-entry PC/instruction FIFO, independent fetch request PC, ready-qualified enqueue, decode-qualified dequeue, and redirect flush/restart behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire io_imemReady into the decoupled frontend and connect FIFO-valid/consume control between fetch, hazard control, and ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace direct instruction-bus backpressure handling with frontend-empty and dequeue control while allowing fetch to run during backend stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_fetch_fifo.py\", \"description\": \"Add cocotb checks for ready-qualified fetches, prefetch during backend stalls, FIFO-empty bubbles, in-order delivery, and complete wrong-path invalidation on redirects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 308.25, \"delta_pct\": 8.99, \"vs_baseline\": 8.99, \"fmax_mhz\": 133.83, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4341607, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9940, \"ff\": 1981, \"seeds\": [133.83, 137.16, 133.6], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:00:58.223364Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1}\n10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"One-entry taken-target instruction replay buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Both earlier predictors reduced CoreMark cycles, but their target selection\\nlogic drove the fetch-address path and destroyed routed Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\nbackward loops repeatedly return to the same first instruction, so retaining\\nthat instruction can recover control-hazard cycles without predicting through\\nthe normal instruction-memory address cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Both earlier predictors reduced CoreMark cycles, but their target selection\\nlogic drove the fetch-address path and destroyed routed Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\nbackward loops repeatedly return to the same first instruction, so retaining\\nthat instruction can recover control-hazard cycles without predicting through\\nthe normal instruction-memory address cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry branch target instruction buffer specialized for a repeatedly\\ntaken backward conditional branch. On the first taken instance, use the\\nexisting EX redirect normally and capture the target instruction when that\\nredirected fetch is accepted. On a later taken instance of the same branch,\\nEX already knows the architectural outcome; replay the registered target\\ninstruction directly into ID/EX and redirect the registered fetch PC to the\\ncached target-plus-four address. This replaces the two wrong-path bubbles with\\nuseful target execution for the hottest loop while making no speculative\\nchange to io_imemAddr and adding no lookup to the sequential PC feedback path.\\n\\nThe entry holds branch-PC and target tags, the target instruction, and the\\ntarget-plus-four address. Fill, replay, and pending-fill state must advance\\nonly on accepted instruction fetches and must remain aligned across imem and\\ndmem stalls. Nonmatching branches, forward branches, jumps, illegal or\\nmisaligned controls, and not-taken outcomes retain the current behavior.\\nEX remains authoritative for direction, traps, RVFI pc_wdata, and recovery,\\nso this optimization cannot execute an unconfirmed target instruction.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact replay payload carrying the cached target instruction, its PC, and valid state into the ID/EX capture path without changing architectural pipeline or RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry backward-branch target instruction buffer with branch and target tags, accepted-fetch fill tracking, EX-confirmed hit detection, and stall-safe state updates.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the replay buffer, connect accepted fetch and resolved branch information, and select the cached target payload for ID/EX only on a confirmed taken hit while preserving the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the accepted fetch PC/instruction for target fill and, on an EX-confirmed replay hit, update the registered PC to cached target-plus-four through the existing redirect update point; keep io_imemAddr driven directly by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a replay input that atomically replaces the wrong-path decode payload with the cached target instruction on a confirmed hit, with reset, flush, load-use, and dmem-stall priorities preventing loss or duplication.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose legal resolved backward-branch PC, target, and taken status, and distinguish normal redirect from a replay hit while leaving architectural pc_next, trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate confirmed replay with redirect flushing so wrong-path fetch/decode state is killed but the injected target instruction is retained, including coincident bus and load-use stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for cold fill, repeated backward-taken replay, branch-tag mismatch, target replacement, not-taken behavior, and replay alignment under imem and dmem backpressure.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact replay payload carrying the cached target instruction, its PC, and valid state into the ID/EX capture path without changing architectural pipeline or RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry backward-branch target instruction buffer with branch and target tags, accepted-fetch fill tracking, EX-confirmed hit detection, and stall-safe state updates.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the replay buffer, connect accepted fetch and resolved branch information, and select the cached target payload for ID/EX only on a confirmed taken hit while preserving the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the accepted fetch PC/instruction for target fill and, on an EX-confirmed replay hit, update the registered PC to cached target-plus-four through the existing redirect update point; keep io_imemAddr driven directly by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a replay input that atomically replaces the wrong-path decode payload with the cached target instruction on a confirmed hit, with reset, flush, load-use, and dmem-stall priorities preventing loss or duplication.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose legal resolved backward-branch PC, target, and taken status, and distinguish normal redirect from a replay hit while leaving architectural pc_next, trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate confirmed replay with redirect flushing so wrong-path fetch/decode state is killed but the injected target instruction is retained, including coincident bus and load-use stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for cold fill, repeated backward-taken replay, branch-tag mismatch, target replacement, not-taken behavior, and replay alignment under imem and dmem backpressure.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 406.58, \"delta_pct\": 0.45, \"vs_baseline\": 43.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 172.65, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10508, \"ff\": 2026, \"seeds\": [195.89, 168.04, 172.65], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:44:48.952189Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r3s2 (improvement, +0.45%): Replaying a cached target instruction only after EX confirms a repeated taken backward branch can recover CoreMark loop bubbles without putting target selection on io_imemAddr, though the small gain shows this narrow one-entry opportunity has limited coverage.\"}\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Hysteretic replacement for the loop replay entry\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The one-entry taken-target replay buffer improved fitness without placing a\\npredictor on the instruction-address timing cone, but every taken backward\\nbranch miss currently starts replacement of the resident entry. Interleaved\\nloop-closing branches can therefore evict the hottest replay entry before it\\nis reused, sharply limiting coverage despite the useful confirmed-replay\\nmechanism already being present.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The one-entry taken-target replay buffer improved fitness without placing a\\npredictor on the instruction-address timing cone, but every taken backward\\nbranch miss currently starts replacement of the resident entry. Interleaved\\nloop-closing branches can therefore evict the hottest replay entry before it\\nis reused, sharply limiting coverage despite the useful confirmed-replay\\nmechanism already being present.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Protect the valid replay entry with a one-candidate, two-strike replacement\\nfilter. A miss by a new backward branch records only its branch PC and target;\\na second miss by that same challenger authorizes the existing accepted-target\\nfill and replaces the resident instruction. A hit clears the challenger so a\\nfrequently reused resident entry is not displaced by isolated or alternating\\nmisses. Initial fill remains immediate when no valid resident exists.\\n\\nThis adds only a candidate tag and a small equality test in the EX-confirmed\\nupdate path. It neither widens the replay payload nor changes io_imemAddr,\\nsequential PC feedback, branch resolution, or RVFI behavior. By eliminating\\ndestructive one-miss thrashing, the same single cached target instruction\\nshould cover more CoreMark loop iterations with negligible routed-Fmax cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-candidate two-strike replacement filter: fill an invalid entry immediately, retain a valid hot entry after an isolated miss, and authorize replacement only when the same branch-PC/target challenger misses again; keep all fill and replay updates qualified by existing accepted-fetch and EX-advance conditions.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed coverage for initial fill, isolated-miss protection, repeated-challenger replacement, challenger cancellation on resident hits, alternating branch sites, and accepted-fetch behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-candidate two-strike replacement filter: fill an invalid entry immediately, retain a valid hot entry after an isolated miss, and authorize replacement only when the same branch-PC/target challenger misses again; keep all fill and replay updates qualified by existing accepted-fetch and EX-advance conditions.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed coverage for initial fill, isolated-miss protection, repeated-challenger replacement, challenger cancellation on resident hits, alternating branch sites, and accepted-fetch behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 316.84, \"delta_pct\": -22.07, \"vs_baseline\": 12.03, \"fmax_mhz\": 134.28, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4238065, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10427, \"ff\": 2088, \"seeds\": [134.28, 132.21, 150.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:03:49.758560Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r4s2 (regression, -22.07%): Adding a second 64-bit branch-PC/target tag and parallel candidate equality to a one-entry replay buffer can collapse routed FPGA Fmax even off io_imemAddr, so narrow CoreMark replacement coverage cannot repay wide tag-comparison and routing cost.\"}\n16:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Branch-PC-only replay-buffer tag\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed replay buffer is the only predictor structure that has\\nimproved fitness, but its hit path compares both a 32-bit branch PC and a\\n32-bit target even though a direct conditional branch's encoded immediate\\nfixes its target for every execution. The redundant target equality consumes\\nLUTs and routing on the EX-confirmed replay decision, where the previous\\ntwo-tag extension showed that wide parallel comparisons can severely reduce\\nrouted Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed replay buffer is the only predictor structure that has\\nimproved fitness, but its hit path compares both a 32-bit branch PC and a\\n32-bit target even though a direct conditional branch's encoded immediate\\nfixes its target for every execution. The redundant target equality consumes\\nLUTs and routing on the EX-confirmed replay decision, where the previous\\ntwo-tag extension showed that wide parallel comparisons can severely reduce\\nrouted Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Match the replay entry using only the full resolved branch PC. Keep the cached\\ntarget PC and target instruction for replay and retain the existing accepted-\\nfetch fill discipline, but remove target equality from hit detection. For an\\nRV32 conditional branch, identical branch PC implies the same instruction and\\ntherefore the same PC-relative target in the immutable benchmark instruction\\nmemory, so this does not introduce aliasing or change architectural behavior.\\n\\nRemoving one 32-bit comparator and its reduction logic should shorten and\\nlighten the confirmed-replay path while preserving the current CoreMark cycle\\nsavings, the registered-PC-only imem address path, all stall behavior, and\\nRVFI semantics. This deliberately improves the proven one-entry mechanism\\ninstead of adding another tag, speculative fetch mux, or PC feedback path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove resolved-target equality from replay hit detection while retaining the cached target for replay payload generation and accepted-fetch fill matching; document why full branch-PC identity is an exact tag for a direct conditional branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that repeated executions of the same branch PC replay correctly, distinct branch PCs never alias even when targets coincide, and fill/replay behavior remains correct under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove resolved-target equality from replay hit detection while retaining the cached target for replay payload generation and accepted-fetch fill matching; document why full branch-PC identity is an exact tag for a direct conditional branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that repeated executions of the same branch PC replay correctly, distinct branch PCs never alias even when targets coincide, and fill/replay behavior remains correct under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 405.12, \"delta_pct\": -6.2, \"vs_baseline\": 43.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 172.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10170, \"ff\": 2028, \"seeds\": [184.81, 168.83, 172.03], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T14:34:14.125484Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Range-compressed replay-buffer PC tags\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry loop replay buffer is the only predictor structure that\\nhas improved fitness, because it recovers a hot control bubble without placing\\ntarget selection on io_imemAddr. Its branch, target, and pending-fill state still\\ncarries and compares full 32-bit addresses even though valid instruction fetches\\nare confined to the aligned 1 MiB executable region.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry loop replay buffer is the only predictor structure that\\nhas improved fitness, because it recovers a hot control bubble without placing\\ntarget selection on io_imemAddr. Its branch, target, and pending-fill state still\\ncarries and compares full 32-bit addresses even though valid instruction fetches\\nare confined to the aligned 1 MiB executable region.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Store and compare only PC[19:2] for the resident branch tag, resident target,\\npending branch tag, and pending target. Reconstruct replay PCs as\\n{12'b0, tag, 2'b00}; alignment and the enforced instruction-address range make\\nthis representation exact rather than probabilistic. Keep both branch-PC and\\ntarget equality, the existing accepted-fetch fill protocol, and the registered\\nPC-only io_imemAddr path unchanged.\\n\\nNarrowing four address registers and both hit/fill comparisons should reduce\\nflip-flop count, equality-reduction depth, and local routing while preserving\\nthe replay buffer's measured CoreMark cycle savings. This avoids the failed\\napproaches of adding entries, removing an exact comparison, or introducing a\\nspeculative target mux on the instruction-fetch timing cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Compress all resident and pending branch/target addresses to aligned 18-bit word tags, reconstruct the full replay PC with zero upper bits, and retain the existing two-tag hit condition and stall-safe fill sequencing.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for compressed-tag hit and miss behavior, boundary addresses within the 1 MiB executable range, distinct word addresses, cold fill, repeated replay, and fill/replay alignment under bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"c