{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r2s0.yaml && rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|yaml.safe_load' Makefile tools schemas | head -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Share unsigned division across RV32M DIV and REM variants\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The ALU expresses signed and unsigned quotient and remainder operations as\n  separate wide division and modulo operators. Since only one RV32M operation\n  executes at a time, parallel signed and unsigned divider fabrics add LUT and\n  routing pressure without increasing throughput, much like the duplicated\n  multipliers removed by the previous winning micro-optimization.\nhypothesis: |\n  Convert both operands to unsigned magnitudes, compute one common unsigned\n  quotient and remainder pair, and apply the RV32M sign rules afterward: negate\n  DIV when operand signs differ, negate REM when the dividend is negative, and\n  leave DIVU/REMU unchanged. Preserve the explicit divide-by-zero and signed\n  overflow results, as well as the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch. Sharing\n  the expensive magnitude arithmetic should reduce divider fabric and routing,\n  improving routed Fmax without changing instruction latency or CoreMark IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Replace separate signed and unsigned DIV/REM expressions with common unsigned magnitude quotient/remainder arithmetic plus compact result sign correction, retaining every RV32M corner case and ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend directed DIV and REM coverage around mixed signs, zero divisors, INT_MIN operands, and the INT_MIN divided by minus one overflow case.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\nto