{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"micro_opt\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct|tostring),(.fitness|tostring),(.fmax_mhz|tostring),(.cycles|tostring),(.lut4|tostring)] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, .implementation_notes, .lesson' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"baseline-bench-7155d3c\tBaseline retest for cores/bench\timprovement\t0.0\t282.82\t127.03\t4491485\t9563\nhyp-20260711-001-r1s0\tShare one multiplier across all RV32M multiply variants\timprovement\t43.11\t404.74\t181.79\t4491485\t10073\nhyp-20260711-001-r2s0\tShare unsigned division across RV32M DIV and REM variants\tregression\t-75.51\t99.12\t44.52\t4491485\t7699\nhyp-20260711-001-r3s0\tGate load-use hazards by actual source operands\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\tnull\tnull\nhyp-20260711-001-r4s0\tExplicit memory byte-lane selection\timprovement\t6.22\t431.88\t183.39\t4246355\t10435\nDecode only the inexpensive opcode-level rs1/rs2 usage predicates for the\ninstruction currently in IF/ID, and qualify each load-use comparison with\nwhether that source is architecturally read. R-type, branches, and stores use\nboth sources; OP-IMM, loads, and JALR use rs1 only; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE,\nand SYSTEM use neither for hazard purposes. This removes false stalls without\naltering true load-use interlocks, forwarding, pipeline latency, retirement,\nor the nret=1 interface. The added gates are local to hazard detection and\nshould improve CoreMark iterations/cycle with little Fmax or area cost.\n\nnull\nnull\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
