emReady is low and advances\\nexactly once using io_dmemRData when readiness returns.\\n\\nReuse the existing EX/MEM forwarding select and substitute raw dmem read data\\nonly when the producer in EX/MEM is an aligned LW; all ALU producers continue\\nto forward the registered ALU result. This removes a common pipeline bubble\\nwith a single local result mux and modest hazard qualification, while leaving\\nretirement, RVFI memory fields, misalignment traps, subword semantics, and the\\nnret=1 interface unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a combinational fast-forward value that selects raw dmem_rdata for a legal aligned word load and the registered ALU result otherwise, without changing load extraction or RVFI capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route the MEM-stage fast-forward value into the existing EX/MEM operand-forwarding input and provide the hazard unit with the load width needed to distinguish fast LW dependencies from subword loads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress the load-use bubble for aligned word-load producers while retaining the current interlock for byte and halfword loads and preserving all redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Document and use the existing EX/MEM forwarding input as a producer result that may come from same-cycle MEM-stage LW data rather than assuming it is always the registered ALU result.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_load_bypass.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that dependent LW consumers execute without a bubble, subword consumers still interlock, and random dmem stalls hold the dependency until ready without stale data, duplicate writes, or duplicate retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stag