{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\nfind cores/bench -maxdepth 4 -type f \\\\( -name '*.rpt' -o -name '*timing*' -o -name '*.json' \\\\) -print | head -100\nfind cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort | tail -30\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r3s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Gate load-use hazards by actual source operands\",\n  \"category\": \"micro_opt\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a pending load destination against both raw\\nsource-register bitfields of every following instruction. Several RV32IM\\nformats do not read one or either of those fields, so immediate bits or a\\ndestination field can accidentally match the load destination and insert a\\nneedless pipeline bubble. CoreMark contains frequent loads followed by\\nimmediate arithmetic, further loads, and control-flow instructions, making\\nthese false dependencies a direct IPC loss under the existing bus-stall model.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector compares a pending load destination against both raw\\nsource-register bitfields of every following instruction. Several RV32IM\\nformats do not read one or either of those fields, so immediate bits or a\\ndestination field can accidentally match the load destination and insert a\\nneedless pipeline bubble. CoreMark contains frequent loads followed by\\nimmediate arithmetic, further loads, and control-flow instructions, making\\nthese false dependencies a direct IPC loss under the existing bus-stall model.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Decode only the inexpensive opcode-level rs1/rs2 usage predicates for the\\ninstruction currently in IF/ID, and qualify each load-use comparison with\\nwhether that source is architecturally read. R-type, branches, and stores use\\nboth sources; OP-IMM, loads, and JALR use rs1 only; JAL, LUI, AUIPC, FENCE,\\nand SYSTEM use neither for hazard purposes. This removes false stalls without\\naltering true load-use interlocks, forwarding, pipeline latency, retirement,\\nor the nret=1 interface. The added gates are local to hazard detection and\\nshould improve CoreMark iterations/cycle with little Fmax or area cost.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 2,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Qualify pending-load rd comparisons with opcode-derived rs1_used and rs2_used predicates so only architectural source operands cause a load-use bubble.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\",\n        \"description\": \"Add directed checks that true load dependencies still stall while false matches in unused instruction fields do not, covering each RV32IM opcode class.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 2,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Qualify pending-load rd comparisons with opcode-derived rs1_used and rs2_used predicates so only architectural source operands cause a load-use bubble.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed checks that true load dependencies still stall while false matches in unused instruction fields do not, covering each RV32IM opcode class.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"broken\",\n  \"formal_passed\": false,\n  \"cosim_passed\": false,\n  \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\n.vcd\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:35  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:35  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 10:34:07 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:35  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engin