rding, and register-state checks expose.\"}\n22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Two-instruction confirmed loop-head replay line\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed branch-target instruction replay buffer is the only\\npredictor design that has improved fitness: it removes a hot loop bubble\\nwithout placing target selection on the instruction-address timing cone.\\nIt currently caches only the first target instruction, so target+4 must still\\nbe fetched normally and is exposed to the benchmark's roughly 22 percent\\ninstruction-memory backpressure. Prior attempts show that another wide tag\\ncomparison is too expensive, but a second data word under the existing tag\\ncan extend useful coverage without another associative lookup.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed branch-target instruction replay buffer is the only\\npredictor design that has improved fitness: it removes a hot loop bubble\\nwithout placing target selection on the instruction-address timing cone.\\nIt currently caches only the first target instruction, so target+4 must still\\nbe fetched normally and is exposed to the benchmark's roughly 22 percent\\ninstruction-memory backpressure. Prior attempts show that another wide tag\\ncomparison is too expensive, but a second data word under the existing tag\\ncan extend useful coverage without another associative lookup.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Turn the existing entry into a two-instruction loop-head replay line sharing\\nthe same exact branch-PC and target tags. During a cold fill, capture both the\\ntarget and target+4 instructions on their respective accepted fetches. On an\\nEX-confirmed hit, inject the target instruction immediately as today, queue\\nthe cached target+4 instruction for the following accepted ID slot, and move\\nthe registered fetch PC directly to target+8. The queued second instruction\\ntherefore hides an instruction-bus stall at target+4 and extends the useful\\nreplay burst without adding any speculative lookup or mux to io_imemAddr.\\n\\nUse an explicit valid/consume handshake for the second replay beat so dmem\\nstalls and load-use hazards hold it without loss or duplication. Hazard\\nsource-address checks must select the pending replay instruction rather than\\nthe simultaneously visible live fetch. Entry validity is published only\\nafter both words have been accepted, and all legal/aligned/backward-branch,\\nexact-tag, RVFI, redirect, and retirement behavior remains unchanged. This\\nadds one 32-bit instruction register and a small replay-phase bit, but no\\nsecond tag, target adder, or parallel equality tree, so it should preserve\\nrouted Fmax while reducing CoreMark cycles under the scored stall model.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the replay payload/control representation for a stallable second cached instruction while leaving architectural pipeline and RVFI fields unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture target and target+4 instructions under one existing exact tag pair, publish the line only after both accepted fills, emit the first word on an EX-confirmed hit, and retain the second word until an explicit ID consume handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire replay-valid/consume control, qualify the second beat against pipeline acceptance, and select replay instruction source fields for load-use detection without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Advance the registered PC to cached target+8 on a confirmed two-word replay and suppress the live target+8 payload while the queued target+4 instruction is being consumed, keeping io_imemAddr driven only by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept each replay beat exactly once, hold the queued second beat across dmem or load-use stalls, and preserve flush and redirect correctness without duplicating retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for two-word fill, ordered replay, target+8 resumption, instruction-bus-stall hiding, second-word load-use hazards, dmem-stall holds, tag misses, and single retirement of each cached instruction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the replay payload/control representation for a stallable second cached instruction while leaving architectural pipeline and RVFI fields unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture target and target+4 instructions under one existing exact tag pair, publish the line only after both accepted fills, emit the first word on an EX-confirmed hit, and retain the second word until an explicit ID consume handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire replay-valid/consume control, qualify the second beat against pipeline acceptance, and select replay instruction source fields for load-use detection without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Advance the registered PC to cached target+8 on a confirmed two-word replay and suppress the live target+8 payload while the queued target+4 instruction is being consumed, keeping io_imemAddr driven only by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept each replay beat exactly once, hold the queued second beat across dmem or load-use stalls, and preserve flush and redirect correctness without duplicating retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for two-word fill, ordered replay, target+8 resumption, instruction-bus-stall hiding, second-word load-use hazards, dmem-stall holds, tag misses, and single retirement of each cached instruction.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.98, \"delta_pct\": -34.25, \"vs_baseline\": 0.41, \"fmax_mhz\": 119.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4193281, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 11070, \"ff\": 2115, \"seeds\": [119.08, 116.54, 121.55], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:15:58.133934Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -34.25%): Extending a confirmed one-word replay entry to target+4 can regress badly even with shared tags, because the phase-controlled 32-bit instruction/PC selection and stall-safe consume/cancel control burden decode and hazard paths more than hiding occasional instruction-memory backpressure repays.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
