{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r4s1.yaml && rg -n \\\"hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|yaml.safe_load\\\" tools schemas Makefile | head -n 60\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"One-entry ordered store buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  A data-bus stall currently freezes every pipeline stage even when the blocked\n  operation is a store whose address and data are already complete. With the\n  evaluation's roughly 22% random dmem backpressure, those store stalls waste\n  execution bandwidth and can combine with later instruction stalls. Earlier\n  structural attempts added timing-sensitive paths to fetch or EX; buffering a\n  completed store confines the new state and arbitration to the MEM boundary.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry write buffer for ordinary RAM stores. When a RAM store reaches\n  MEM while io_dmemReady is low, capture its address, replicated data, and byte\n  enables, allow that store to advance to retirement, and let following\n  non-memory instructions continue while the buffer drains. If a younger load\n  or store reaches MEM before the entry drains, hold it behind the buffered\n  store rather than adding load forwarding or permitting memory reordering.\n\n  UART and timing-marker writes in the 0x10000000-0x10000200 window remain\n  unbuffered and retire only on an actual bus handshake. The buffered request\n  has priority on the external dmem port, is issued exactly once, and may be\n  replaced by a waiting RAM store only after the older entry is accepted. This\n  should recover cycles from isolated store backpressure while leaving the ALU,\n  operand-forwarding, and instruction-address timing cones unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry RAM-store queue with capture, stable drain request, single-handshake completion, and explicit empty/full state.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Arbitrate buffered stores onto dmem, enqueue stalled ordinary-RAM stores, keep MMIO stores strongly ordered, and expose whether the current memory operation may advance.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace raw store backpressure freezing with a MEM-stage blocked indication so non-memory instructions can proceed while a queued store drains, while younger memory operations remain ordered.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the store-buffer advance/block controls into the existing pipeline hold network without changing the nret=1 interface or RVFI retirement ordering.\"\n  - file: test/test_store_buffer.py\n    description: \"Check stalled-store capture and single issue, progress of following non-memory instructions, blocking of younger memory operations, random-stall ordering, and unbuffered UART/marker behavior.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:161:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:185:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:218:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:235:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/orchestrator.py:606:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:338:        data = yaml.safe_load(raw)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:            data = yaml.safe_load(repaired)\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/bench/runner.py:99:    cfg = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
