{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'from tools.orchestrator import validate_hypothesis; h=validate_hypothesis(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml\\\"); print(h[\\\"id\\\"], h[\\\"category\\\"], h[\\\"expected_impact\\\"])'\ngit diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml\ngit status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml\nsed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/bonetto/.matplotlib is not a writable directory\nMatplotlib created a temporary cache directory at /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/.tmp/matplotlib-v70l2e6m because there was an issue with the default path (/Users/bonetto/.matplotlib); it is highly recommended to set the MPLCONFIGDIR environment variable to a writable directory, in particular to speed up the import of Matplotlib and to better support multiprocessing.\n\nFontconfig error: No writable cache directories\n\t/opt/homebrew/var/cache/fontconfig\n\t/Users/bonetto/.cache/fontconfig\n\t/Users/bonetto/.fontconfig\nMatplotlib is building the font cache; this may take a moment.\nhyp-20260711-002-r9s1 structural {'fitness_delta_pct': 4, 'confidence': 'medium'}\nid: hyp-20260711-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Collapse MEM and WB into direct commit\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage pipeline carries a wide MEM/WB payload for every\n  instruction and keeps a second writeback forwarding source on both EX operand\n  muxes. The register exists mainly to delay retirement by one cycle: EX/MEM\n  already holds all architectural metadata, and the memory stage already forms\n  the final load value, masks, trap state, and writeback value combinationally.\n  On the Tang Nano fabric, deleting a pipeline boundary and a forwarding tier is\n  a promising way to reduce both routed state and ordinary-instruction mux depth.\nhypothesis: |\n  Convert the core to IF-ID-EX/MEM-commit by making the memory stage a purely\n  combinational completion block over the held EX/MEM entry. An instruction\n  commits directly when EX/MEM is valid and either is not a memory operation or\n  its dmem handshake is ready; a stalled memory entry remains held exactly as it\n  is today and cannot retire or write twice. Feed the final commit value to the\n  register file's existing write-first port and drive RVFI directly from the\n  same completion bundle, then remove the MEM/WB register, WB stage, and MEM/WB\n  operand-forwarding tier.\n\n  Preserve the current one-cycle load-use interlock. Thus a load result crosses\n  only into register-file writeback and same-edge ID capture, never directly\n  into the following instruction's EX ALU cone; immediate ALU dependencies still\n  use the registered EX/MEM bypass, while dependencies two positions back see\n  the direct commit through the existing write-first register-file behavior.\n  This should leave steady-state CoreMark IPC and bus semantics unchanged while\n  removing hundreds of pipeline flops, their routing, and one 32-bit input from\n  each EX forwarding mux, increasing routed Fmax without speculative frontend\n  logic, new global interlocks, or any change to the nret=1 contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace the registered MEM/WB payload with a compact combinational commit bundle containing final writeback, RVFI, memory-mask, trap, and valid fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the MEM/WB register and emit a ready-qualified combinational completion bundle from EX/MEM, preserving fixed lane selection, alignment traps, memory masks, and exact single-handshake commit semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Retire and write the register file directly from the completion bundle, increment RVFI order only on commit, remove MEM/WB and WB-stage wiring, and keep dmem-stalled EX/MEM entries held until ready.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Reduce each EX operand selector to registered EX/MEM forwarding versus the ID/EX value, deleting the MEM/WB comparison and select encoding while retaining x0 and youngest-writer rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the reduced two-source forwarding selection without adding completion data or dmem input to the execute datapath.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retain the load-use bubble and EX/MEM dmem hold, but remove MEM/WB hold generation because completion valid is directly qualified by dmem readiness.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Delete the obsolete standalone WB stage after its final-result selection and write qualification move into the direct commit path.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add directed checks for ALU and load dependency distances, write-first commit-to-ID capture, memory stalls, single store issue, single retirement, RVFI order, and load or misalignment trap behavior in the four-stage topology.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
