olved architectural next PC differs from that prediction. Correct loop\n  and direct-call predictions therefore avoid the existing two-younger-instruction\n  flush, while wrong predictions recover through the existing redirect path.\n\n  Keep prediction combinational and stateless: recognize the B-type opcode plus\n  legal funct3 and use the immediate sign bit for backward-taken, recognize JAL,\n  form each target directly from instruction bits, and require word alignment.\n  EX remains authoritative for branch conditions, JALR targets, misalignment\n  traps, and RVFI pc_wdata. Redirect must retain priority over all bus stalls, and\n  prediction metadata must remain attached to a held instruction so random imem\n  and dmem backpressure cannot cause stale or duplicate execution.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with predicted-next-PC metadata so each instruction carries the exact fetch decision that EX must validate.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add decode-light BTFNT conditional-branch and direct-JAL prediction, advance the PC to aligned predicted targets, preserve redirect-over-stall priority, and emit the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX with the same stall and flush behavior as the instruction, PC, operands, and valid bit.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC against the carried prediction and assert redirect only on mismatch, while preserving JALR recovery and all existing misalignment-trap and RVFI pc_wdata semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat redirect as misprediction recovery rather than every taken control transfer, preserving the existing flush, load-use, and bus-backpressure priorities.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed checks for backward taken and not-taken branches, forward branches, direct JAL, JALR fallback, misaligned targets, and recovery coincident with imem or dmem stalls.\"\nYAML structure and paths: valid\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
