behavior. By eliminating\\ndestructive one-miss thrashing, the same single cached target instruction\\nshould cover more CoreMark loop iterations with negligible routed-Fmax cost.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 2, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv', 'description': 'Add a one-candidate two-strike replacement filter: fill an invalid entry immediately, retain a valid hot entry after an isolated miss, and authorize replacement only when the same branch-PC/target challenger misses again; keep all fill and replay updates qualified by existing accepted-fetch and EX-advance conditions.'}, {'file': 'test/test_predictor.py', 'description': 'Add directed coverage for initial fill, isolated-miss protection, repeated-challenger replacement, challenger cancellation on resident hits, alternating branch sites, and accepted-fetch behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.'}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
