{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"hypothesis\\\\.schema|jsonschema|yaml.safe_load\\\" tools Makefile schemas | head -n 80 && sed -n '1,240p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"tools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/orchestrator.py:606:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:161:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:185:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:218:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/test_hypothesis.py:235:    data = _yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:338:        data = yaml.safe_load(raw)\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:351:            data = yaml.safe_load(repaired)\ntools/bench/runner.py:99:    cfg = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nid: hyp-20260711-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Two-instruction confirmed loop-head replay line\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The one-entry confirmed branch-target instruction replay buffer is the only\n  predictor design that has improved fitness: it removes a hot loop bubble\n  without placing target selection on the instruction-address timing cone.\n  It currently caches only the first target instruction, so target+4 must still\n  be fetched normally and is exposed to the benchmark's roughly 22 percent\n  instruction-memory backpressure. Prior attempts show that another wide tag\n  comparison is too expensive, but a second data word under the existing tag\n  can extend useful coverage without another associative lookup.\nhypothesis: |\n  Turn the existing entry into a two-instruction loop-head replay line sharing\n  the same exact branch-PC and target tags. During a cold fill, capture both the\n  target and target+4 instructions on their respective accepted fetches. On an\n  EX-confirmed hit, inject the target instruction immediately as today, queue\n  the cached target+4 instruction for the following accepted ID slot, and move\n  the registered fetch PC directly to target+8. The queued second instruction\n  therefore hides an instruction-bus stall at target+4 and extends the useful\n  replay burst without adding any speculative lookup or mux to io_imemAddr.\n\n  Use an explicit valid/consume handshake for the second replay beat so dmem\n  stalls and load-use hazards hold it without loss or duplication. Hazard\n  source-address checks must select the pending replay instruction rather than\n  the simultaneously visible live fetch. Entry validity is published only\n  after both words have been accepted, and all legal/aligned/backward-branch,\n  exact-tag, RVFI, redirect, and retirement behavior remains unchanged. This\n  adds one 32-bit instruction register and a small replay-phase bit, but no\n  second tag, target adder, or parallel equality tree, so it should preserve\n  routed Fmax while reducing CoreMark cycles under the scored stall model.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the replay payload/control representation for a stallable second cached instruction while leaving architectural pipeline and RVFI fields unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Capture target and target+4 instructions under one existing exact tag pair, publish the line only after both accepted fills, emit the first word on an EX-confirmed hit, and retain the second word until an explicit ID consume handshake.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire replay-valid/consume control, qualify the second beat against pipeline acceptance, and select replay instruction source fields for load-use detection without changing the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Advance the registered PC to cached target+8 on a confirmed two-word replay and suppress the live target+8 payload while the queued target+4 instruction is being consumed, keeping io_imemAddr driven only by the PC register.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept each replay beat exactly once, hold the queued second beat across dmem or load-use stalls, and preserve flush and redirect correctness without duplicating retirement.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed checks for two-word fill, ordered replay, target+8 resumption, instruction-bus-stall hiding, second-word load-use hazards, dmem-stall holds, tag misses, and single retirement of each cached instruction.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
