{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-004-r14s0.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-004-r14s0.yaml && rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|safe_load' tools Makefile | head -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-004-r14s0\ntitle: \"Replay-aligned source-qualified load-use hazard\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The load-use detector treats both register-shaped instruction fields as consumed\n  sources for every opcode. Accidental matches therefore insert bubbles after loads\n  even when the following instruction does not read rs1 or rs2. The previous rs2-only\n  qualification attempt targeted this useful CPI opportunity but became incorrect\n  when branch replay replaced the live IF instruction without replacing the opcode\n  used by hazard detection.\nhypothesis: |\n  Derive the hazard register tags and compact uses-rs1/uses-rs2 qualifiers from the\n  exact instruction selected by ID after replay arbitration, then require a load\n  destination match only for sources that instruction actually consumes. OP, STORE,\n  and BRANCH consume rs2; OP, OP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR consume rs1.\n  Replay and ordinary fetch will consequently use one coherent instruction identity.\n\n  This should eliminate false load-use bubbles without forwarding memory data into\n  EX, changing pipeline latency, or adding state. Keeping the opcode classification\n  beside the existing ID selection and sending only two qualifier bits plus the\n  already-selected register tags to the hazard unit minimizes timing and routing\n  risk while preserving every true dependency, bus stall, trap, RVFI, and nret=1\n  behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose hazard rs1/rs2 tags and compact source-use qualifiers derived from the same replay-selected instruction that decode and the register file consume.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the replay-aligned ID hazard metadata into the load-use detector instead of using raw live IF instruction fields, preserving all existing pipeline handshakes.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate each load destination comparison with its selected instruction source-use bit while retaining true load dependencies and the existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add directed ordinary-fetch and replay cases proving true rs1/rs2 dependencies bubble and non-source field matches do not, including OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, and SYSTEM encodings.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/eval/formal.py:32:    y = yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:152:    y = yaml.safe_load(yaml_path.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:365:                    y = yaml.safe_load(candidate.read_text()) or {}\ntools/orchestrator.py:446:        hyp = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/orchestrator.py:606:        y = yaml.safe_load((src / \"core.yaml\").read_text()) or {}\ntools/test_core_yaml_update.py:24:    y = yaml.safe_load((core_dir / \"core.yaml\").read_text())\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/bench/runner.py:99:    cfg = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text())\ntools/agents/implement.py:170:        hypothesis = yaml.safe_load(f)\ntools/agents/test_hyp