{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-004-r14s0\\\") | {id,title,hypothesis:.hypothesis.hypothesis,changes,outcome,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,lut4,error,implementation_notes,lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r7s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Canonicalize unused source operands before hazard detection\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Have the validated decoder identify whether each instruction actually uses\\nrs1 and rs2, then present x0 as the address and zero as the value for every\\nunused source before the ID/EX register. Feed these canonical source addresses\\nto the existing load-use equality checks instead of raw instruction fields.\\nTrue dependencies retain the same one-cycle interlock, while false matches\\ndisappear and unused RVFI source fields remain self-consistent with x0.\\n\\nThis should reduce CoreMark cycles without adding qualifier gates after the\\nhazard comparators or changing forwarding, pipeline latency, bus behavior,\\nretirement, illegal-instruction trapping, or the nret=1 interface. Source-use\\nbits must default false and only assert within validated decoder arms so the\\ndefault-illegal discipline remains intact.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Emit validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 controls for each legal RV32IM instruction class, defaulting both false for illegal and source-free instructions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Canonicalize unused register addresses and values to x0/zero before register-file reads and ID/EX capture so execution and RVFI observe the same source contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Drive load-use detection from the ID stage's canonical source addresses rather than raw IF instruction bitfields, preserving replay and stall priorities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Rename and document the source inputs as canonical architectural addresses while retaining the existing shallow equality-based load-use logic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Check true dependencies, false matches in unused fields, canonical RVFI source fields, illegal encodings, replay, and coincident instruction/data bus stalls.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"broken\",\n  \"delta_pct\": null,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": null,\n  \"lut4\": null,\n  \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\",\n  \"implementation_notes\": null,\n  \"lesson\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Prune post-execute pipeline payloads\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Introduce stage-specific compact control payloads and remove resolved-branch\\nmetadata after it has produced pc_next and the replay-buffer signals in EX.\\nEX/MEM will retain only memory, writeback, and trap controls; MEM/WB will retain\\nonly register-write, result-select, and trap controls. This is an end-to-end\\ndeletion of unused state with no new mux, comparator, interlock, or fetch-PC\\nfeedback and no change to instruction timing, CoreMark cycles, RVFI fields,\\nbus-stall behavior, or nret. Reducing pipeline-register width and control fanout\\nshould improve placement and routed Fmax while also lowering FF and LUT use.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"delta_pct\": -5.79,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 185.56,\n  \"lut4\": 10185,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"lesson\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r14s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Replay-aligned source-qualified load-use hazard\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Derive the hazard register tags and compact uses-rs1/uses-rs2 qualifiers from the\\nexact instruction selected by ID after replay arbitration, then require a load\\ndestination match only for sources that instruction actually consumes. OP, STORE,\\nand BRANCH consume rs2; OP, OP-IMM, LOAD, STORE, BRANCH, and JALR consume rs1.\\nReplay and ordinary fetch will consequently use one coherent instruction identity.\\n\\nThis should eliminate false load-use bubbles without forwarding memory data into\\nEX, changing pipeline latency, or adding state. Keeping the opcode classification\\nbeside the existing ID selection and sending only two qualifier bits plus the\\nalready-selected register tags to the hazard unit minimizes timing and routing\\nrisk while preserving every true dependency, bus stall, trap, RVFI, and nret=1\\nbehavior.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Expose hazard rs1/rs2 tags and compact source-use qualifiers derived from the same replay-selected instruction that decode and the register file consume.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire the replay-aligned ID hazard metadata into the load-use detector instead of using raw live IF instruction fields, preserving all existing pipeline handshakes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Gate each load destination comparison with its selected instruction source-use bit while retaining true load dependencies and the existing redirect and bus-stall priorities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_hazard.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed ordinary-fetch and replay cases proving true rs1/rs2 dependencies bubble and non-source field matches do not, including OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, and SYSTEM encodings.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"broken\",\n  \"delta_pct\": null,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": null,\n  \"lut4\": null,\n  \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\",\n  \"implementation_notes\": null,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-004-r14s0 (broken, n/a): Replay-aligned load-use detection is still unsafe when replay.valid has priority over flush/stall in the ID/EX register, because a detected dependency cannot inject its required bubble; replay capture must obey the same interlock as ordinary decode.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
