l/cores/bench-15381/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): Falling-edge register-file writeback is half a cycle too late for an ID instruction that captures operands on the same rising edge its producer reaches MEM/WB, so removing the WB-to-ID write-first bypass requires an interlock or an earlier architectural write point.\"}\n21:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Registered instruction-response boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current frontend presents io_imemData combinationally to instruction\\ndecode, immediate generation, register-file address selection, and the\\nID/EX capture edge. That couples the wrapper instruction memory's output\\npath to a wide decode/read cone. The previous autonomous two-entry fetch\\nFIFO paid heavily for independent-PC control and queue routing, but it did\\nnot isolate the simpler opportunity to retime the instruction response\\nwhile leaving io_imemAddr on the existing registered-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current frontend presents io_imemData combinationally to instruction\\ndecode, immediate generation, register-file address selection, and the\\nID/EX capture edge. That couples the wrapper instruction memory's output\\npath to a wide decode/read cone. The previous autonomous two-entry fetch\\nFIFO paid heavily for independent-PC control and queue routing, but it did\\nnot isolate the simpler opportunity to retime the instruction response\\nwhile leaving io_imemAddr on the existing registered-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Insert one explicit IF/ID response register carrying PC, instruction, and\\nvalid. Capture it only when io_imemReady is asserted and decode can advance;\\nhold both it and the fetch PC through load-use or dmem stalls, and invalidate\\nit synchronously on an EX redirect. Decode and register-file reads then start\\nfrom local flops instead of directly from io_imemData, splitting the current\\nmemory-to-ID/EX timing cone without an autonomous request PC, FIFO occupancy\\narithmetic, or a new mux on io_imemAddr.\\n\\nThe added stage preserves one-instruction-per-cycle steady-state throughput\\nbut adds one wrong-path slot to redirect recovery. Retain the confirmed\\nbackward-branch replay path as an ID/EX injection so hot loop hits still\\nbypass the newly registered frontend slot, and explicitly discard any held\\nwrong-path response when replay or redirect wins. The expected routed-Fmax\\ngain from this clean pipeline cut should outweigh the modest extra cycles\\nfor non-replayed taken branches and jumps while preserving nret=1 retirement,\\nRVFI ordering, precise traps, and all bus-stall semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Redefine the IF/ID payload as an explicitly registered frontend boundary while retaining PC, instruction, and valid metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry ready-qualified IF/ID response register, hold it and the PC in lockstep under downstream stalls, and synchronously invalidate wrong-path contents on redirects or replay without adding autonomous fetch control to io_imemAddr.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the registered IF/ID payload and preserve replay as the higher-priority direct ID/EX injection, with precise hold and flush behavior for the added frontend stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive frontend capture/hold and ID advancement from response-valid, load-use, redirect, and dmem-stall conditions rather than treating io_imemReady as a combinational decode-valid signal.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered response boundary and its consume control while retaining the PC-only instruction-address path, existing replay buffer, pipeline ordering, and nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_id_register.py\", \"description\": \"Add cycle-accurate tests for ready-qualified capture, sustained one-per-cycle flow, held responses, redirect and replay invalidation, load-use interaction, and coincident randomized instruction/data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Redefine the IF/ID payload as an explicitly registered frontend boundary while retaining PC, instruction, and valid metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry ready-qualified IF/ID response register, hold it and the PC in lockstep under downstream stalls, and synchronously invalidate wrong-path contents on redirects or replay without adding autonomous fetch control to io_imemAddr.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the registered IF/ID payload and preserve replay as the higher-priority direct ID/EX injection, with precise hold and flush behavior for the added frontend stage.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive frontend capture/hold and ID advancement from response-valid, load-use, redirect, and dmem-stall conditions rather than treating io_imemReady as a combinational decode-valid signal.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the registered response boundary and its consume control while retaining the PC-only instruction-address path, existing replay buffer, pipeline ordering, and nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_if_id_register.py\", \"description\": \"Add cycle-accurate tests for ready-qualified capture, sustained one-per-cycle flow, held responses, redirect and replay invalidation, load-use interaction, and coincident randomized instruction/data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: liveness_c