 carry control and data long after their\\nlast consumer. In particular, EX/MEM retains branch outcome and target fields\\nthat no downstream stage reads, and both EX/MEM and MEM/WB forward the complete\\ndecode control record even though execute-only ALU and control-flow bits are\\ndead. At the current high Fmax, these unnecessary flops and wide inter-stage\\nroutes can increase placement congestion and clock-enable fanout without\\nimproving IPC or architectural observability.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the uniform carried-forward control record with stage-specific control\\npayloads. Keep the full decoded control only in ID/EX; EX/MEM will retain only\\nmemory, writeback, and trap controls, while MEM/WB will retain only the controls\\nneeded for final writeback and rvfi_trap. Remove EX/MEM branch_taken and\\nbranch_target after branch resolution because pc_next already captures the\\narchitectural outcome and the replay buffer consumes its resolved signals\\ndirectly from EX.\\n\\nPreserve every RVFI operand, PC, instruction, memory, and result field through\\nthe existing registered retirement boundary, and preserve the exact reset,\\nflush, dmem-hold, forwarding, and single-retirement behavior. Construct each\\nnarrower payload directly at its producing stage so this change deletes state\\nand routing rather than adding decode or selection logic to active datapaths.\\nCoreMark cycles should therefore remain unchanged while reduced pipeline width\\nand control fanout improve routed median Fmax on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define stage-specific EX/MEM and MEM/WB control records, remove dead post-EX branch outcome fields, and retain every field required by forwarding, memory behavior, writeback, and RVFI.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate only the narrowed EX/MEM memory, writeback, and trap 