ization must canonicalize the full source contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Have the validated decoder identify whether each instruction actually uses\\nrs1 and rs2, then present x0 as the address and zero as the value for every\\nunused source before the ID/EX register. Feed these canonical source addresses\\nto the existing load-use equality checks instead of raw instruction fields.\\nTrue dependencies retain the same one-cycle interlock, while false matches\\ndisappear and unused RVFI source fields remain self-consistent with x0.\\n\\nThis should reduce CoreMark cycles without adding qualifier gates after the\\nhazard comparators or changing forwarding, pipeline latency, bus behavior,\\nretirement, illegal-instruction trapping, or the nret=1 interface. Source-use\\nbits must default false and only assert within validated decoder arms so the\\ndefault-illegal discipline remains intact.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit validated uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 controls for each legal RV32IM instruction class, defaulting both false for illegal and source-free instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Canonicalize unused register addresses and values to x0/zero before register-file reads and ID/EX capture so execution and RVFI observe the same source contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Drive load-use detection from the ID stage's canonical source addresses rather than raw IF instruction bitfields, preserving replay and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Rename and document the source inputs as canonical architectural addresses while retaining the existing shallow equality-based load-use logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Check true dependencies, false matches in unused fields, canonical RVFI source fields, illegal encodings, replay, 