{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r4s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260711-003-r9s2\\\") | {id,title,hypothesis:.hypothesis.hypothesis,changes,implementation_notes,cycles,fmax_mhz,lut4,ff}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r4s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Hysteretic replacement for the loop replay entry\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Protect the valid replay entry with a one-candidate, two-strike replacement\\nfilter. A miss by a new backward branch records only its branch PC and target;\\na second miss by that same challenger authorizes the existing accepted-target\\nfill and replaces the resident instruction. A hit clears the challenger so a\\nfrequently reused resident entry is not displaced by isolated or alternating\\nmisses. Initial fill remains immediate when no valid resident exists.\\n\\nThis adds only a candidate tag and a small equality test in the EX-confirmed\\nupdate path. It neither widens the replay payload nor changes io_imemAddr,\\nsequential PC feedback, branch resolution, or RVFI behavior. By eliminating\\ndestructive one-miss thrashing, the same single cached target instruction\\nshould cover more CoreMark loop iterations with negligible routed-Fmax cost.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a one-candidate two-strike replacement filter: fill an invalid entry immediately, retain a valid hot entry after an isolated miss, and authorize replacement only when the same branch-PC/target challenger misses again; keep all fill and replay updates qualified by existing accepted-fetch and EX-advance conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed coverage for initial fill, isolated-miss protection, repeated-challenger replacement, challenger cancellation on resident hits, alternating branch sites, and accepted-fetch behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"cycles\": 4238065,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 134.28,\n  \"lut4\": 10427,\n  \"ff\": 2088\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r9s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Two-strike replay-entry admission\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Add one miss-history bit implementing two-strike admission for a valid replay\\nentry. A confirmed eligible miss immediately after a replay hit preserves the\\ncurrent entry and merely arms replacement; a second eligible miss before the\\nnext hit may start the existing accepted-fetch fill and replace the entry. Any\\nreplay hit clears the armed bit, while an invalid entry still fills on its\\nfirst eligible miss so cold-start behavior remains fast.\\n\\nThis policy should keep a hot CoreMark loop head resident across isolated\\ntaken branches and reduce destructive one-entry thrashing. It adds no target\\nstate, comparator, instruction mux, replay phase, or logic on io_imemAddr; the\\nreplay hit equation and all pipeline, stall, trap, RVFI, and nret=1 behavior\\nremain unchanged. If execution moves to a new phase, two eligible misses are\\nsufficient to admit its target, bounding the loss from stale-entry retention.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a single replacement-armed bit and two-strike admission policy around the existing miss-to-fill state update, with immediate first fill when the entry is invalid and hit-based re-protection, while leaving the exact-target replay hit path unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold first-miss fill, preservation after one isolated conflicting miss, replacement after two misses without an intervening hit, hit-based re-protection, and identical behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"cycles\": 4236949,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 136.43,\n  \"lut4\": 10211,\n  \"ff\": 1961\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
