{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-006-r14s2.yaml && rg -n 'hypothesis.schema|jsonschema|validate.*hypothesis' Makefile tools cores/bench -g '*.py' -g 'Makefile' | head -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-006-r14s2\ntitle: \"One-bit hysteretic replay-entry replacement\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The confirmed backward-branch replay entry improves this core, but every\n  exact-target miss immediately displaces the resident loop head. In nested\n  loops, an infrequent outer-loop backedge can therefore evict the frequently\n  reused inner-loop target just before execution returns to that inner loop.\n  A second candidate or victim tag is too expensive on this FPGA, but a single\n  replacement-protection bit can distinguish a proven hot entry without adding\n  another wide comparator or target register.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one-bit replacement hysteresis to the existing exact-target replay entry.\n  Set the protection bit whenever the resident entry hits. On the first miss\n  against a protected entry, retain the entry, clear protection, and do not\n  start a fill; a subsequent hit restores protection, while a subsequent miss\n  may replace the entry through the existing pending-fill protocol. Invalid or\n  unprotected entries continue to fill exactly as they do today.\n\n  This policy keeps a repeatedly useful inner-loop instruction resident across\n  a single intervening outer-loop branch, yet eventually admits a new loop after\n  workload phase changes. It adds only one flop and local control, keeps the\n  exact 32-bit resident-target match, and adds no lookup, target mux, metadata,\n  or combinational logic to io_imemAddr. Replay remains EX-confirmed, so wrong\n  instructions are never injected and architectural control flow, stalls,\n  traps, RVFI ordering, and the nret=1 interface remain unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit hit-protection state and hysteretic miss replacement: retain a proven resident entry across one miss, re-protect it on a hit, and otherwise use the existing stall-safe pending-fill protocol unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add directed nested-loop and phase-change checks covering hit protection, first-miss retention, hit re-protection, second-miss replacement, cold fill, and behavior across instruction and data stalls.\"\ntools/tournament.py:54:# The hypothesis schema's `category` enum, in the order the brief specifies.\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:220:        emit_verilog, offlimits_changes, _read_notes, validate_hypothesis,\ntools/tournament.py:261:        hyp = validate_hypothesis(hyp_path)\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:444:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\ntools/agents/static_agent.py:94:        \"      No-op placeholder to satisfy the hypothesis schema's\\n\"\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
