ngine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 14:01:18 [liveness_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: liveness_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 14:01:18 [liveness_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_liveness_check_sv_38_58 at rvfi_liveness_check.sv:38.5-38.28 step 20\\nSBY 14:01:18 [liveness_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1/formal/last_run-53177.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-sol-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260711-002-r7s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-53177/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r7s1 (broken, n/a): Registering the IF/ID instruction response is an elastic-buffer protocol change, not a pure retime; request-PC advance, response valid, decode consume/refill, and redirect/replay invalidation must be tracked independently or instructions can be dropped or stranded, as the liveness, PC-forwarding, and register-state checks expose.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Two-instruction confirmed loop-head replay line\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed branch-target instruction replay buffer is the only\\npredictor design that has improved fitness: it removes a hot loop bubble\\nwithout placing target selection on the instruction-address timing cone.\\nIt currently caches only the first target instruction, so target+4 must still\\nbe fetched normally and is exposed to the benchmark's roughly 22 percent\\ninstruction-memory backpressure. Prior attempts show that another wide tag\\ncomparison is too expensive, but a second data word under the existing tag\\ncan extend useful coverage without another associative lookup.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The one-entry confirmed branch-target instruction replay buffer is the only\\npredictor design that has improved fitness: it removes a hot loop bubble\\nwithout placing target selection on the instruction-address timing cone.\\nIt currently caches only the first target instruction, so target+4 must still\\nbe fetched normally and is exposed to the benchmark's roughly 22 percent\\ninstruction-memory backpressure. Prior attempts show that another wide tag\\ncomparison is too expensive, but a second data word under the existing tag\\ncan extend useful coverage without another associative lookup.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Turn the existing entry into a two-instruction loop-head replay line sharing\\nthe same exact branch-PC and target tags. During a cold fill, capture both the\\ntarget and target+4 instructions on their respective accepted fetches. On an\\nEX-confirmed hit, inject the target instruction immediately as today, queue\\nthe cached target+4 instruction for the following accepted ID slot, and move\\nthe registered fetch PC directly to target+8. The queued second instruction\\ntherefore hides an instruction-bus stall at target+4 and extends the useful\\nreplay burst without adding any speculative lookup or mux to io_imemAddr.\\n\\nUse an explicit valid/consume handshake for the second replay beat so dmem\\nstalls and load-use hazards hold it without loss or duplication. Hazard\\nsource-address checks must select the pending replay instruction rather than\\nthe simultaneously visible live fetch. Entry validity is published only\\nafter both words have been accepted, and all legal/aligned/backward-branch,\\nexact-tag, RVFI, redirect, and retirement behavior remains unchanged. This\\nadds one 32-bit instruction register and a small replay-phase bit, but no\\nsecond tag, target adder, or parallel equality tree, so it should preserve\\nrouted Fmax while reducing CoreMark cycles under the scored stall model.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the replay payload/control representation for a stallable second cached instruction while leaving architectural pipeline and RVFI fields unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture target and target+4 instructions under one existing exact tag pair, publish the line only after both accepted fills, emit the first word on an EX-confirmed hit, and retain the second word until an explicit ID consume handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire replay-valid/consume control, qualify the second beat against pipeline acceptance, and select replay instruction source fields for load-use detection without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Advance the registered PC to cached target+8 on a confirmed two-word replay and suppress the live target+8 payload while the queued target+4 instruction is being consumed, keeping io_imemAddr driven only by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept each replay beat exactly once, hold the queued second beat across dmem or load-use stalls, and preserve flush and redirect correctness without duplicating retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for two-word fill, ordered replay, target+8 resumption, instruction-bus-stall hiding, second-word load-use hazards, dmem-stall holds, tag misses, and single retirement of each cached instruction.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the replay payload/control representation for a stallable second cached instruction while leaving architectural pipeline and RVFI fields unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Capture target and target+4 instructions under one existing exact tag pair, publish the line only after both accepted fills, emit the first word on an EX-confirmed hit, and retain the second word until an explicit ID consume handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire replay-valid/consume control, qualify the second beat against pipeline acceptance, and select replay instruction source fields for load-use detection without changing the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Advance the registered PC to cached target+8 on a confirmed two-word replay and suppress the live target+8 payload while the queued target+4 instruction is being consumed, keeping io_imemAddr driven only by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept each replay beat exactly once, hold the queued second beat across dmem or load-use stalls, and preserve flush and redirect correctness without duplicating retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for two-word fill, ordered replay, target+8 resumption, instruction-bus-stall hiding, second-word load-use hazards, dmem-stall holds, tag misses, and single retirement of each cached instruction.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 283.98, \"delta_pct\": -34.25, \"vs_baseline\": 0.41, \"fmax_mhz\": 119.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4193281, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 11070, \"ff\": 2115, \"seeds\": [119.08, 116.54, 121.55], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:15:58.133934Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r7s2 (regression, -34.25%): Extending a confirmed one-word replay entry to target+4 can regress badly even with shared tags, because the phase-controlled 32-bit instruction/PC selection and stall-safe consume/cancel control burden decode and hazard paths more than hiding occasional instruction-memory backpressure repays.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:23:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Target-only replay-buffer tag\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry replay buffer is the only control-flow optimization\\nthat has improved the current core, but each hit compares both the owning\\nbranch PC and the cached target PC. The payload is simply the instruction at\\nthat target, so the branch-PC identity is redundant: any legal, aligned,\\ntaken backward branch resolving to the same target can safely reuse it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-entry replay buffer is the only control-flow optimization\\nthat has improved the current core, but each hit compares both the owning\\nbranch PC and the cached target PC. The payload is simply the instruction at\\nthat target, so the branch-PC identity is redundant: any legal, aligned,\\ntaken backward branch resolving to the same target can safely reuse it.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the stored branch-PC tag, its pending-fill copy, and the parallel\\n32-bit branch-PC equality from the replay-buffer hit path. Retain the exact\\n32-bit target comparison, captured target instruction, confirmed-EX lookup,\\naccepted-fetch fill protocol, and target-plus-four resume behavior unchanged.\\nThis is a strict hardware reduction with no new muxes or qualifiers, and\\nshould reduce comparator fabric, flops, and routing on the replay decision\\nwhile modestly broadening reuse when multiple backward branches share a loop\\nhead. Architectural execution, stalls, RVFI, traps, and nret remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the entry and pending branch-PC tags and qualify confirmed replay hits solely with the existing exact target-PC tag and eligibility signals, preserving fill and replay timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused resolved branch-PC output while retaining legal aligned taken-backward qualification and the exact resolved target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant resolved-branch-PC wiring and update the replay-buffer connection without changing pipeline, bus-stall, or nret=1 behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that same-target backward branches reuse one cached instruction, different targets miss and refill, and replay remains single-shot and stall-safe.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the entry and pending branch-PC tags and qualify confirmed replay hits solely with the existing exact target-PC tag and eligibility signals, preserving fill and replay timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the now-unused resolved branch-PC output while retaining legal aligned taken-backward qualification and the exact resolved target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the redundant resolved-branch-PC wiring and update the replay-buffer connection without changing pipeline, bus-stall, or nret=1 behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks that same-target backward branches reuse one cached instruction, different targets miss and refill, and replay remains single-shot and stall-safe.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 463.86, \"delta_pct\": 7.4, \"vs_baseline\": 64.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 196.97, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10217, \"ff\": 1956, \"seeds\": [186.25, 197.01, 196.97], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:40:47.746851Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r8s0 (improvement, +7.40%): A confirmed backward-branch replay entry is safely keyed by its exact target alone, so dropping the redundant branch-PC tag removes 32-bit comparator, flop, and routing cost while allowing branches that share a loop head to reuse the cached instruction.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"B-immediate tag for confirmed branch replay\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-instruction replay buffer is the only predictor structure that\\nhas improved fitness, but every hit currently requires both a full 32-bit branch-PC\\nequality and a second full 32-bit resolved-target equality. The target comparison\\nis wider than necessary because an RV32I conditional branch target is completely\\ndetermined by its 12 encoded B-immediate bits plus the already-compared branch PC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed one-instruction replay buffer is the only predictor structure that\\nhas improved fitness, but every hit currently requires both a full 32-bit branch-PC\\nequality and a second full 32-bit resolved-target equality. The target comparison\\nis wider than necessary because an RV32I conditional branch target is completely\\ndetermined by its 12 encoded B-immediate bits plus the already-compared branch PC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the replay entry's 32-bit target tag comparison with an exact comparison of\\nthe branch instruction's B-immediate bits [12:1]. EX will export these bits directly\\nfrom the already-latched decoded immediate, and the replay buffer will store them\\nwhen a confirmed miss begins a fill. A hit will require the unchanged full branch-PC\\nmatch plus the 12-bit displacement match, while the stored full target PC remains\\navailable solely to label the cached instruction and advance fetch to target+4.\\n\\nThis is an exact tag transformation for legal conditional branches: branch PC and\\nB-immediate uniquely determine the resolved target, including backward offsets, so\\nhit behavior, CoreMark cycles, redirects, stalls, RVFI state, and illegal/misaligned\\nhandling remain unchanged. Removing 20 comparator bits and their routed resolved-\\ntarget inputs from the replay-hit cone should raise FPGA Fmax without adding fetch-PC\\nfeedback logic, replay phases, range guards, or another entry.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Export the exact B-immediate displacement tag from the valid legal conditional branch in EX alongside the existing resolved branch PC and target signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact resolved displacement tag between EX and the confirmed replay buffer without changing the nret=1 interface or any hazard and redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Store and compare the 12-bit B-immediate tag instead of comparing the full 32-bit target tag, while retaining the full target PC for fill matching, replay PC, and target-plus-four resumption.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed alias checks showing that identical branch PCs with different positive and negative B-immediates miss, while exact displacement matches replay correctly across instruction and data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Export the exact B-immediate displacement tag from the valid legal conditional branch in EX alongside the existing resolved branch PC and target signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact resolved displacement tag between EX and the confirmed replay buffer without changing the nret=1 interface or any hazard and redirect priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Store and compare the 12-bit B-immediate tag instead of comparing the full 32-bit target tag, while retaining the full target PC for fill matching, replay PC, and target-plus-four resumption.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed alias checks showing that identical branch PCs with different positive and negative B-immediates miss, while exact displacement matches replay correctly across instruction and data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 450.2, \"delta_pct\": 4.24, \"vs_baseline\": 59.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 191.17, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10248, \"ff\": 2052, \"seeds\": [195.96, 191.17, 189.5], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:34:13.579251Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r8s2 (regression, +4.24%): Replacing a replay buffer's resolved-target equality with a B-immediate tag can regress despite the narrower comparator because it adds EX-to-buffer routing and duplicate tag state while the full target must still be retained, so tag compression only pays when it removes information end to end.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Prune post-execute pipeline payloads\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM register still carries resolved branch_taken and branch_target values\\nthat no downstream stage consumes, and the full execute control bundle is copied\\nthrough EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though most fields are dead after EX. These wide,\\nfrequently toggling registers consume flops and routing on an FPGA where routed\\nFmax now dominates fitness.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Introduce stage-specific compact control payloads and remove resolved-branch\\nmetadata after it has produced pc_next and the replay-buffer signals in EX.\\nEX/MEM will retain only memory, writeback, and trap controls; MEM/WB will retain\\nonly register-write, result-select, and trap controls. This is an end-to-end\\ndeletion of unused state with no new mux, comparator, interlock, or fetch-PC\\nfeedback and no change to instruction timing, CoreMark cycles, RVFI fields,\\nbus-stall behavior, or nret. Reducing pipeline-register width and control fanout\\nshould improve placement and routed Fmax while also lowering FF and LUT use.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact EX/MEM and MEM/WB control types, replace the full ctrl_t fields in downstream payloads, and delete unused registered branch_taken and branch_target fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pack only memory, writeback, and trap controls into EX/MEM and stop registering branch outcome metadata after redirect, pc_next, and replay qualification have been computed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM control, propagate only retirement-relevant writeback and trap bits into MEM/WB, and preserve all alignment, memory-mask, held-forwarding, and RVFI semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, retirement, and trap references for the stage-specific control payloads without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline timing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select and qualify register writeback from the compact MEM/WB control payload with behavior identical to the existing full-control path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 436.99, \"delta_pct\": -5.79, \"vs_baseline\": 54.51, \"fmax_mhz\": 185.56, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10185, \"ff\": 1971, \"seeds\": [179.92, 185.56, 198.93], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:52:35.726601Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Two-strike replay-entry admission\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The exact-target one-instruction replay buffer is the only predictor structure\\nthat has improved fitness, but its replace-on-every-miss policy lets a single\\ncold taken backward branch evict a frequently reused loop-head instruction.\\nAdding capacity or another identity tag has already imposed much more FPGA\\ntiming cost than CoreMark recovered, so replacement policy is the remaining\\nway to improve effective coverage without widening the replay datapath.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The exact-target one-instruction replay buffer is the only predictor structure\\nthat has improved fitness, but its replace-on-every-miss policy lets a single\\ncold taken backward branch evict a frequently reused loop-head instruction.\\nAdding capacity or another identity tag has already imposed much more FPGA\\ntiming cost than CoreMark recovered, so replacement policy is the remaining\\nway to improve effective coverage without widening the replay datapath.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one miss-history bit implementing two-strike admission for a valid replay\\nentry. A confirmed eligible miss immediately after a replay hit preserves the\\ncurrent entry and merely arms replacement; a second eligible miss before the\\nnext hit may start the existing accepted-fetch fill and replace the entry. Any\\nreplay hit clears the armed bit, while an invalid entry still fills on its\\nfirst eligible miss so cold-start behavior remains fast.\\n\\nThis policy should keep a hot CoreMark loop head resident across isolated\\ntaken branches and reduce destructive one-entry thrashing. It adds no target\\nstate, comparator, instruction mux, replay phase, or logic on io_imemAddr; the\\nreplay hit equation and all pipeline, stall, trap, RVFI, and nret=1 behavior\\nremain unchanged. If execution moves to a new phase, two eligible misses are\\nsufficient to admit its target, bounding the loss from stale-entry retention.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single replacement-armed bit and two-strike admission policy around the existing miss-to-fill state update, with immediate first fill when the entry is invalid and hit-based re-protection, while leaving the exact-target replay hit path unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold first-miss fill, preservation after one isolated conflicting miss, replacement after two misses without an intervening hit, hit-based re-protection, and identical behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single replacement-armed bit and two-strike admission policy around the existing miss-to-fill state update, with immediate first fill when the entry is invalid and hit-based re-protection, while leaving the exact-target replay hit path unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold first-miss fill, preservation after one isolated conflicting miss, replacement after two misses without an intervening hit, hit-based re-protection, and identical behavior under instruction and data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 322.0, \"delta_pct\": -30.58, \"vs_baseline\": 13.85, \"fmax_mhz\": 136.43, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4236949, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10211, \"ff\": 1961, \"seeds\": [119.22, 157.06, 136.43], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T17:50:50.397008Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Valid-only reset for pipeline payload banks\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"ID/EX, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB synchronously clear every bit of their wide packed\\npayloads even though invalid entries are architecturally ignored. This puts\\nreset and flush selection on hundreds of PC, instruction, operand, result,\\nand RVFI-data flops, increasing global control fanout and placement pressure\\nin a design whose fitness is now dominated by routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"ID/EX, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB synchronously clear every bit of their wide packed\\npayloads even though invalid entries are architecturally ignored. This puts\\nreset and flush selection on hundreds of PC, instruction, operand, result,\\nand RVFI-data flops, increasing global control fanout and placement pressure\\nin a design whose fitness is now dominated by routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split each pipeline register into a small validity/control bank and a wide\\ndata bank. Reset and bubble flushes clear only valid plus the control bits\\nneeded to suppress register writes, memory requests, forwarding, and traps;\\ndata fields retain or capture don't-care values while invalid and never\\nacquire a reset/flush mux. Keep the existing stall and MEM/WB held-forwarding\\nbehavior exactly intact. Unlike the failed register-file valid-mask attempt,\\nthis adds no lookup or select to an active operand path: validity already\\nqualifies retirement and side effects. Removing reset/flush fanout from the\\nwide payload flops should improve placement and median Fmax without changing\\nCoreMark cycles, pipeline latency, bus handshakes, RVFI semantics, or nret.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor ID/EX into separately clocked control-valid and data banks so reset and flush invalidate the entry without clearing PC, instruction, immediate, register tags, or operand payloads; preserve replay and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor EX/MEM so reset clears valid and side-effect controls only, while the wide execute and RVFI payload bank has no reset mux and continues to hold on data-memory stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor MEM/WB into valid, control, and payload banks, retaining the existing hold behavior needed for forwarding while removing reset from wide result, memory, instruction, PC, and operand fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline_reset.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed reset, redirect-flush, load-use bubble, replay, and data-stall checks proving invalid payload values cannot retire, write registers, issue memory requests, perturb forwarding, or violate RVFI once a valid instruction arrives.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor ID/EX into separately clocked control-valid and data banks so reset and flush invalidate the entry without clearing PC, instruction, immediate, register tags, or operand payloads; preserve replay and stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor EX/MEM so reset clears valid and side-effect controls only, while the wide execute and RVFI payload bank has no reset mux and continues to hold on data-memory stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor MEM/WB into valid, control, and payload banks, retaining the existing hold behavior needed for forwarding while removing reset from wide result, memory, instruction, PC, and operand fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline_reset.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed reset, redirect-flush, load-use bubble, replay, and data-stall checks proving invalid payload values cannot retire, write registers, issue memory requests, perturb forwarding, or violate RVFI once a valid instruction arrives.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 402.27, \"delta_pct\": -13.28, \"vs_baseline\": 42.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 170.82, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10010, \"ff\": 1957, \"seeds\": [170.82, 170.56, 173.25], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:16:52.246722Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-001-r10s0 (regression, -13.28%): Splitting packed pipeline registers into separate valid/control and unreset payload always_ff banks can cost more in FPGA register-control packing and routing than it saves in reset fanout, so valid-only reset is not automatically a timing win for wide ID/EX, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB payloads.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed shared PC-relative target adder\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Every taken conditional branch currently closes a 32-bit path from the ID/EX\\nPC and immediate through an EX-stage target adder and redirect selection back\\nto the fetch PC. CoreMark repeatedly exercises backward branches, while prior\\nresults show that adding prediction or buffering to the fetch path sacrifices\\ntoo much routed Fmax. The ID stage already has both the instruction PC and its\\ndecoded immediate before the ID/EX boundary, so this addition need not remain\\non the branch-resolution feedback cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Every taken conditional branch currently closes a 32-bit path from the ID/EX\\nPC and immediate through an EX-stage target adder and redirect selection back\\nto the fetch PC. CoreMark repeatedly exercises backward branches, while prior\\nresults show that adding prediction or buffering to the fetch path sacrifices\\ntoo much routed Fmax. The ID stage already has both the instruction PC and its\\ndecoded immediate before the ID/EX boundary, so this addition need not remain\\non the branch-resolution feedback cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute one shared PC-plus-immediate value combinationally in ID and register\\nit alongside each instruction in ID/EX. Use that registered value in EX for\\nconditional-branch targets, direct-JAL targets, and AUIPC results; retain the\\nexisting forwarded rs1-plus-immediate adder only for JALR. This retimes the\\nwide PC-relative addition across the ID/EX boundary and removes it from the\\nhigh-frequency EX-to-fetch redirect path without changing branch latency,\\nprediction policy, instruction count, or any bus handshake.\\n\\nThe registered sum must follow the instruction through every existing hold,\\nflush, replay, and reset case. EX remains authoritative for branch condition,\\nJALR bit-zero clearing, target-alignment traps, redirect qualification, and\\nRVFI pc_wdata. Sharing the retimed value with AUIPC also prevents synthesis\\nfrom retaining a redundant PC-relative adder. The expected result is higher\\nmedian Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles, for a net fitness improvement with\\nonly 32 additional pipeline bits and no new global control or fetch-PC mux.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative sum to the ID/EX payload so the value remains aligned with its instruction across stalls, flushes, and replay injection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Form one selected-PC-plus-immediate sum and capture it in every normal and replay ID/EX update while preserving the existing reset, hold, and bubble semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered sum for branch and direct-JAL targets and AUIPC writeback, leaving only JALR's operand-dependent addition in EX and preserving redirect, alignment-trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add dependency- and stall-aware checks for taken and untaken branches, JAL, JALR, AUIPC, replay, target misalignment, and RVFI next-PC behavior after the PC-relative adder retime.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered PC-relative sum to the ID/EX payload so the value remains aligned with its instruction across stalls, flushes, and replay injection.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Form one selected-PC-plus-immediate sum and capture it in every normal and replay ID/EX update while preserving the existing reset, hold, and bubble semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered sum for branch and direct-JAL targets and AUIPC writeback, leaving only JALR's operand-dependent addition in EX and preserving redirect, alignment-trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add dependency- and stall-aware checks for taken and untaken branches, JAL, JALR, AUIPC, replay, target misalignment, and RVFI next-PC behavior after the PC-relative adder retime.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 422.03, \"delta_pct\": -9.02, \"vs_baseline\": 49.22, \"fmax_mhz\": 179.21, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10363, \"ff\": 1990, \"seeds\": [190.22, 179.21, 153.99], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:19:59.820672Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r10s1 (regression, -9.02%): Retiming the shared 32-bit PC-plus-immediate adder from EX into combinational ID can merely trade the redirect cone for a decode-to-ID/EX path plus 32 routed payload bits, so PC-relative target precomputation is not a timing win unless the added decode and pipeline-routing cost is cheaper.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Direction-agnostic confirmed branch replay\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The exact-target, one-instruction confirmed replay buffer is the only predictor\\nstructure that has improved this core, but it currently excludes every taken\\nforward conditional branch and spends a full-width comparison deciding whether\\nthe resolved target is below the branch PC. CoreMark repeats forward as well as\\nbackward control decisions inside loops, so this restriction leaves useful\\nreplay opportunities uncovered while retaining direction logic in EX.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The exact-target, one-instruction confirmed replay buffer is the only predictor\\nstructure that has improved this core, but it currently excludes every taken\\nforward conditional branch and spends a full-width comparison deciding whether\\nthe resolved target is below the branch PC. CoreMark repeats forward as well as\\nbackward control decisions inside loops, so this restriction leaves useful\\nreplay opportunities uncovered while retaining direction logic in EX.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Admit every valid, legal, aligned, taken conditional branch to the existing\\nexact-target replay buffer, irrespective of displacement direction. A matching\\nentry will replay the cached target instruction only after EX confirms the\\nbranch is taken, exactly as today; misses will use the unchanged accepted-fetch\\nfill protocol. Remove the branch_target < branch_pc comparison and replace the\\nresolved_taken_backward interface with a simple resolved_taken qualification.\\n\\nThis broadens dynamic coverage and deletes a 32-bit magnitude comparator without\\nadding tags, entries, history bits, instruction mux levels, or any selection on\\nio_imemAddr. EX remains authoritative, so not-taken branches, illegal encodings,\\nmisaligned targets, redirects, bus stalls, RVFI ordering, and retirement behavior\\nremain unchanged. The expected gain comes from both fewer repeated forward-branch\\nbubbles and reduced execute-to-replay timing and routing cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace backward-only replay eligibility with a valid legal aligned taken-conditional-branch signal, eliminating the full-width target-versus-PC direction comparison while leaving redirect and trap resolution authoritative.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the direction-agnostic confirmed-taken signal from EX to the existing replay buffer without changing the nret=1 interface, hazard priorities, or fetch-address path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Allow the unchanged exact-target hit and accepted-fetch fill protocol to operate for taken forward and backward conditional branches, with no added predictor state or datapath width.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for repeated taken forward branches, alternating taken and not-taken outcomes, exact-target conflicts, misaligned targets, and replay behavior across imem and dmem stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace backward-only replay eligibility with a valid legal aligned taken-conditional-branch signal, eliminating the full-width target-versus-PC direction comparison while leaving redirect and trap resolution authoritative.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the direction-agnostic confirmed-taken signal from EX to the existing replay buffer without changing the nret=1 interface, hazard priorities, or fetch-address path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Allow the unchanged exact-target hit and accepted-fetch fill protocol to operate for taken forward and backward conditional branches, with no added predictor state or datapath width.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for repeated taken forward branches, alternating taken and not-taken outcomes, exact-target conflicts, misaligned targets, and replay behavior across imem and dmem stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 191.82, \"delta_pct\": -58.65, \"vs_baseline\": -32.18, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.65, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4256598, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10714, \"ff\": 1955, \"seeds\": [88.79, 81.17, 81.65], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T18:14:04.794042Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r10s2 (regression, -58.65%): Admitting taken forward branches to a one-entry exact-target replay buffer makes every confirmed miss replace its pending or hot target, so CoreMark's forward control flow can thrash the high-value backward-loop entry despite removing the EX direction comparator.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:33:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-005-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Two-stage partial-product multiplier sidecar\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Sharing the MUL-family hardware produced the largest improvement in the\\ntournament, which strongly suggests that the remaining 32x32 combinational\\nproduct and its routing still materially constrain the execute-stage Fmax.\\nThe current ALU forms the complete 64-bit product and signed-high corrections\\nin the same cycle as every ordinary ALU operation, even though only\\nMUL-family instructions need that structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Sharing the MUL-family hardware produced the largest improvement in the\\ntournament, which strongly suggests that the remaining 32x32 combinational\\nproduct and its routing still materially constrain the execute-stage Fmax.\\nThe current ALU forms the complete 64-bit product and signed-high corrections\\nin the same cycle as every ordinary ALU operation, even though only\\nMUL-family instructions need that structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extract MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU from the common combinational ALU into a\\nfixed-latency two-stage multiplier sidecar. On dispatch, register four\\nunsigned 16x16 partial products plus the operand sign-correction metadata;\\nin the following cycle, combine the registered partials into the exact\\n64-bit unsigned product, apply the existing high-half signedness corrections,\\nand inject the saved instruction into EX/MEM exactly once. This creates a\\nhard pipeline cut inside the 32x32 multiply rather than merely registering\\nits already-computed result, and removes multiplier outputs from the normal\\nALU result case cone.\\n\\nA MUL-family dispatch holds younger IF/ID state for the single completion\\ncycle, while older EX/MEM work drains normally; if dmem backpressure blocks\\ncompletion, the sidecar retains its registered request and result metadata\\nuntil EX/MEM accepts it. Keep non-M instructions on the existing one-cycle\\nexecute path with unchanged forwarding, branch resolution, memory behavior,\\nand retirement. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, retain the current one-cycle\\nalgebraic stand-ins so bounded formal depth and semantics are unchanged.\\nThe expected Fmax gain from shorter DSP/LUT and routing depth should exceed\\nthe CoreMark cost of one extra cycle on MUL-family instructions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/multiplier.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stallable two-stage MUL-family sidecar that registers four unsigned 16x16 partial products, combines them exactly into one 64-bit product, applies signed-high corrections, and exposes a single ready/accept completion handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove production MUL-family arithmetic from the ordinary combinational result cone while preserving the exact existing one-cycle RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and all non-M ALU behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define the compact saved MUL request metadata needed to preserve destination, PC, instruction, operands, control, and RVFI source values until sidecar completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch MUL-family instructions into the sidecar only when EX/MEM can advance, suppress their ordinary EX/MEM write, and arbitrate each registered completion into EX/MEM exactly once without changing the normal execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fixed-latency MUL dispatch/completion interlock with dmem-stall priority, holding younger fetch/decode state without duplicating or dropping the resident instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the multiplier-sidecar handshake and localized pipeline hold signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface, forwarding rules, RVFI order, and existing replay behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_multiplier.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized cycle-aware checks for all MUL variants, partial-product carry boundaries, mixed-sign high halves, dependent consumers, single retirement, and completion held across instruction/data bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/multiplier.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stallable two-stage MUL-family sidecar that registers four unsigned 16x16 partial products, combines them exactly into one 64-bit product, applies signed-high corrections, and exposes a single ready/accept completion handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove production MUL-family arithmetic from the ordinary combinational result cone while preserving the exact existing one-cycle RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and all non-M ALU behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define the compact saved MUL request metadata needed to preserve destination, PC, instruction, operands, control, and RVFI source values until sidecar completion.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Dispatch MUL-family instructions into the sidecar only when EX/MEM can advance, suppress their ordinary EX/MEM write, and arbitrate each registered completion into EX/MEM exactly once without changing the normal execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the fixed-latency MUL dispatch/completion interlock with dmem-stall priority, holding younger fetch/decode state without duplicating or dropping the resident instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the multiplier-sidecar handshake and localized pipeline hold signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface, forwarding rules, RVFI order, and existing replay behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_multiplier.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed and randomized cycle-aware checks for all MUL variants, partial-product carry boundaries, mixed-sign high halves, dependent consumers, single retirement, and completion held across instruction/data bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 218.63, \"delta_pct\": -52.87, \"vs_baseline\": -22.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 94.89, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340258, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 11178, \"ff\": 2316, \"seeds\": [94.89, 89.75, 96.86], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:12:34.841280Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-005-r11s1 (regression, -52.87%): Splitting a mapper-optimized 32x32 product into four registered 16x16 partials does not isolate timing when their wide recombination/correction still feeds an EX/MEM completion mux and mul_dispatch enters centralized fetch/decode stalls, so a multiplier sidecar must decouple both its result and interlock paths from ordinary cycles.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-006-r11s2\", \"title\": \"In-place refill tag for confirmed branch replay\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed backward-branch instruction replay buffer is the only predictor\\ndesign that has improved fitness, and its best subsequent result came from\\ndeleting redundant identity state. During a miss refill, the current buffer\\nnevertheless stores the same 32-bit target in both the resident entry tag and\\na separate pending-fill tag, adding flops, comparison, muxing, and routing to\\na design whose fitness is now highly sensitive to routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed backward-branch instruction replay buffer is the only predictor\\ndesign that has improved fitness, and its best subsequent result came from\\ndeleting redundant identity state. During a miss refill, the current buffer\\nnevertheless stores the same 32-bit target in both the resident entry tag and\\na separate pending-fill tag, adding flops, comparison, muxing, and routing to\\na design whose fitness is now highly sensitive to routed Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"On an eligible confirmed miss, invalidate the resident instruction and write\\nthe resolved target directly into its existing target-tag register, using\\nfill_pending only to distinguish an incomplete entry. Match the redirected,\\naccepted fetch against that resident tag and revalidate the entry when its\\ninstruction is captured. This removes fill_target_pc_q and its duplicate\\nequality/update network end to end while leaving hit identity, replacement\\npolicy, backward-only eligibility, replay timing, and CoreMark cycles intact.\\n\\nA miss already redirects and flushes all younger instructions, so the old\\nentry cannot produce a useful confirmed hit before the redirected target is\\naccepted. Give a newer same-cycle miss priority over completion of an older\\npending fill so stale fetch data can never validate under a new tag. The\\nchange adds no state, prediction metadata, fetch-address mux, or PC feedback\\nlogic and should improve placement and median Fmax without altering bus-stall,\\ntrap, RVFI, or nret=1 behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the invalid resident target register as the pending refill tag, delete fill_target_pc_q and its duplicate compare/update paths, and enforce newer-miss priority over stale fill completion while preserving the exact confirmed-replay behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold and replacement refills, accepted-fetch qualification through stalls, miss-time invalidation, and simultaneous stale-fill completion plus a newer miss, including exact-target hit and reset behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Reuse the invalid resident target register as the pending refill tag, delete fill_target_pc_q and its duplicate compare/update paths, and enforce newer-miss priority over stale fill completion while preserving the exact confirmed-replay behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold and replacement refills, accepted-fetch qualification through stalls, miss-time invalidation, and simultaneous stale-fill completion plus a newer miss, including exact-target hit and reset behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 366.2, \"delta_pct\": -21.05, \"vs_baseline\": 29.48, \"fmax_mhz\": 155.5, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10596, \"ff\": 1934, \"seeds\": [166.03, 150.42, 155.5], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:05:45.763631Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Range-qualified narrow replay target tags\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The confirmed backward-branch replay buffer still stores and compares full\\n32-bit target addresses even though every permitted instruction access lies\\nin the aligned 1 MiB executable window. A prior compression attempt lost its\\nbenefit by repeatedly rechecking upper bits inside the buffer; the current\\ntarget-only design makes it possible to enforce that condition once upstream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The confirmed backward-branch replay buffer still stores and compares full\\n32-bit target addresses even though every permitted instruction access lies\\nin the aligned 1 MiB executable window. A prior compression attempt lost its\\nbenefit by repeatedly rechecking upper bits inside the buffer; the current\\ntarget-only design makes it possible to enforce that condition once upstream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Qualify replay eligibility in EX with branch_target[31:20] equal to zero,\\nthen carry only the aligned word index branch_target[19:2] into the replay\\nbuffer. Store resident and pending targets as 18-bit tags, compare accepted\\nfetches and confirmed hits using only PC[19:2], and reconstruct replay.pc and\\nreplay_next_pc with constant zero upper and low bits. Because an entry can be\\ncreated only after the single upstream range check, the buffer needs no local\\nupper-bit or alignment guards; out-of-range branches simply use the unchanged\\narchitectural redirect path and never populate or hit replay state.\\n\\nThis deletes 28 target-state bits and narrows both replay equality networks\\nwithout adding a fetch-address mux, pipeline field, or recurring guard. It\\nshould preserve CoreMark cycles, exact in-range identity, stalls, traps, RVFI,\\nand nret=1 behavior while modestly improving placement and routed Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the sole executable-range qualification to legal aligned taken-backward branch replay eligibility and expose the 18-bit aligned target tag while leaving architectural redirects unrestricted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow resolved target tag into the replay buffer without changing the top-level interface, pipeline control, or instruction-memory address path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace both full-width resident and pending target registers and their comparisons with 18-bit word tags, reconstruct full replay PCs from constants, and add no local range guards.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Check exact narrow-tag fill and replay at executable-range boundaries, exclusion of out-of-range targets, replacement, and accepted-fetch behavior across bus stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the sole executable-range qualification to legal aligned taken-backward branch replay eligibility and expose the 18-bit aligned target tag while leaving architectural redirects unrestricted.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the narrow resolved target tag into the replay buffer without changing the top-level interface, pipeline control, or instruction-memory address path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace both full-width resident and pending target registers and their comparisons with 18-bit word tags, reconstruct full replay PCs from constants, and add no local range guards.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Check exact narrow-tag fill and replay at executable-range boundaries, exclusion of out-of-range targets, replacement, and accepted-fetch behavior across bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 428.41, \"delta_pct\": -7.64, \"vs_baseline\": 51.48, \"fmax_mhz\": 181.92, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10242, \"ff\": 1960, \"seeds\": [181.92, 180.08, 194.17], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:34:11.461579Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-004-r12s0 (regression, -7.64%): Narrowing replay targets to PC[19:2] still loses when the required branch_target[31:20] range qualification is inserted into EX branch-valid control, so moving address guards upstream can trade comparator width for timing pressure on a more critical branch-resolution cone.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:36:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-005-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Stage-specialized narrow pipeline payloads\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current packed pipeline bundles carry control and data long after their\\nlast consumer. In particular, EX/MEM retains branch outcome and target fields\\nthat no downstream stage reads, and both EX/MEM and MEM/WB forward the complete\\ndecode control record even though execute-only ALU and control-flow bits are\\ndead. At the current high Fmax, these unnecessary flops and wide inter-stage\\nroutes can increase placement congestion and clock-enable fanout without\\nimproving IPC or architectural observability.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current packed pipeline bundles carry control and data long after their\\nlast consumer. In particular, EX/MEM retains branch outcome and target fields\\nthat no downstream stage reads, and both EX/MEM and MEM/WB forward the complete\\ndecode control record even though execute-only ALU and control-flow bits are\\ndead. At the current high Fmax, these unnecessary flops and wide inter-stage\\nroutes can increase placement congestion and clock-enable fanout without\\nimproving IPC or architectural observability.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the uniform carried-forward control record with stage-specific control\\npayloads. Keep the full decoded control only in ID/EX; EX/MEM will retain only\\nmemory, writeback, and trap controls, while MEM/WB will retain only the controls\\nneeded for final writeback and rvfi_trap. Remove EX/MEM branch_taken and\\nbranch_target after branch resolution because pc_next already captures the\\narchitectural outcome and the replay buffer consumes its resolved signals\\ndirectly from EX.\\n\\nPreserve every RVFI operand, PC, instruction, memory, and result field through\\nthe existing registered retirement boundary, and preserve the exact reset,\\nflush, dmem-hold, forwarding, and single-retirement behavior. Construct each\\nnarrower payload directly at its producing stage so this change deletes state\\nand routing rather than adding decode or selection logic to active datapaths.\\nCoreMark cycles should therefore remain unchanged while reduced pipeline width\\nand control fanout improve routed median Fmax on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define stage-specific EX/MEM and MEM/WB control records, remove dead post-EX branch outcome fields, and retain every field required by forwarding, memory behavior, writeback, and RVFI.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate only the narrowed EX/MEM memory, writeback, and trap controls while keeping resolved branch signals local to redirect and replay handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM controls and register only the MEM/WB writeback and trap controls, preserving alignment traps, held-load forwarding data, masks, and retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, writeback, and RVFI wiring for the stage-specialized control types without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline handshakes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the compact MEM/WB writeback controls while preserving the existing final-result mux and register-file write qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline_payloads.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks across ALU, branch, jump, load, store, illegal, misaligned, forwarding, and random bus-stall cases to prove narrowed payloads preserve side effects, RVFI fields, ordering, and single retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define stage-specific EX/MEM and MEM/WB control records, remove dead post-EX branch outcome fields, and retain every field required by forwarding, memory behavior, writeback, and RVFI.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate only the narrowed EX/MEM memory, writeback, and trap controls while keeping resolved branch signals local to redirect and replay handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrowed EX/MEM controls and register only the MEM/WB writeback and trap controls, preserving alignment traps, held-load forwarding data, masks, and retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Update hazard, forwarding, writeback, and RVFI wiring for the stage-specialized control types without changing the nret=1 interface or pipeline handshakes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the compact MEM/WB writeback controls while preserving the existing final-result mux and register-file write qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline_payloads.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks across ALU, branch, jump, load, store, illegal, misaligned, forwarding, and random bus-stall cases to prove narrowed payloads preserve side effects, RVFI fields, ordering, and single retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 414.9, \"delta_pct\": -10.55, \"vs_baseline\": 46.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 176.18, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10310, \"ff\": 1959, \"seeds\": [172.62, 194.17, 176.18], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:31:18.058416Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-006-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Dedicated direct-JAL target instruction replay\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The exact-target backward-branch replay entry is the only predictor structure\\nthat has improved this core, because it recovers a control bubble without\\nselecting a speculative address onto io_imemAddr. CoreMark also repeatedly\\ncalls the same helper functions with direct JAL instructions, but admitting\\nthose targets to the branch entry would evict valuable loop-head state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The exact-target backward-branch replay entry is the only predictor structure\\nthat has improved this core, because it recovers a control bubble without\\nselecting a speculative address onto io_imemAddr. CoreMark also repeatedly\\ncalls the same helper functions with direct JAL instructions, but admitting\\nthose targets to the branch entry would evict valuable loop-head state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a second, independently filled one-word replay entry specialized for legal,\\naligned direct JAL targets. On the first occurrence, retain the ordinary EX\\nredirect and capture the target instruction only when that redirected fetch is\\naccepted. On a later exact-target hit, inject the registered function-entry\\ninstruction into ID/EX after EX confirms the JAL and advance the registered PC\\nto target plus four, using the same non-speculative replay protocol as the\\nproven backward-branch entry.\\n\\nKeeping JAL state in a dedicated entry prevents repeated calls from replacing\\nthe hot conditional-loop entry and avoids the forward-branch thrashing seen in\\nprior experiments. Qualify the two hit comparators by mutually exclusive EX\\ncontrol classes and select only a confirmed replay, so no lookup or target mux\\nreaches io_imemAddr or the sequential PC feedback cone. EX remains authoritative\\nfor legality, alignment, resolved next PC, traps, and RVFI; JALR remains on the\\nnormal redirect path. The expected IPC gain from recurring CoreMark calls may\\noutweigh the modest additional registered entry and class-gated comparison.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/jal_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry accepted-fetch-filled instruction replay buffer for legal aligned direct-JAL targets, with exact-target confirmed hits and stall-safe pending-fill state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a valid legal aligned direct-JAL resolution class and target for replay lookup while leaving JALR, misalignment traps, redirect authority, and RVFI next-PC semantics unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the dedicated JAL replay entry, arbitrate mutually exclusive confirmed branch/JAL replay payloads into the existing ID and PC replay interfaces, and preserve the nret=1 contract and accepted-fetch qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold and repeated direct-JAL calls, branch-entry isolation, same-target calls from different PCs, JALR exclusion, misaligned targets, and replay/fill behavior across instruction and data stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/jal_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a one-entry accepted-fetch-filled instruction replay buffer for legal aligned direct-JAL targets, with exact-target confirmed hits and stall-safe pending-fill state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a valid legal aligned direct-JAL resolution class and target for replay lookup while leaving JALR, misalignment traps, redirect authority, and RVFI next-PC semantics unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the dedicated JAL replay entry, arbitrate mutually exclusive confirmed branch/JAL replay payloads into the existing ID and PC replay interfaces, and preserve the nret=1 contract and accepted-fetch qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for cold and repeated direct-JAL calls, branch-entry isolation, same-target calls from different PCs, JALR exclusion, misaligned targets, and replay/fill behavior across instruction and data stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 158.75, \"delta_pct\": -65.78, \"vs_baseline\": -43.87, \"fmax_mhz\": 67.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4225638, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10850, \"ff\": 2079, \"seeds\": [67.05, 69.02, 67.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T19:28:49.644421Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:38:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-004-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Opcode-qualified load-use rs2 hazard\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector currently compares a load destination against both\\ninstruction fields [19:15] and [24:20] for every following instruction.\\nFor OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, and SYSTEM encodings,\\n[24:20] is not a consumed rs2 register, so an accidental tag match inserts\\na needless bubble. CoreMark contains frequent load and immediate-operation\\nsequences, making these false dependencies a direct iterations-per-cycle\\nloss under the existing random bus-stall workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector currently compares a load destination against both\\ninstruction fields [19:15] and [24:20] for every following instruction.\\nFor OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL, FENCE, and SYSTEM encodings,\\n[24:20] is not a consumed rs2 register, so an accidental tag match inserts\\na needless bubble. CoreMark contains frequent load and immediate-operation\\nsequences, making these false dependencies a direct iterations-per-cycle\\nloss under the existing random bus-stall workload.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Qualify only the rs2 half of load-use detection with a compact opcode check\\nthat is true for the three instruction classes that actually consume rs2:\\nOP, STORE, and BRANCH. Keep the existing rs1 comparison unchanged because\\nit covers the common base/source operand classes, and retain a real bubble\\nfor every true load-to-OP, load-to-store-data, or load-to-branch dependency.\\n\\nThis removes false stalls without forwarding io_dmemRData into EX, changing\\npipeline latency, or adding state. Restricting the change to one local gate\\non the already-existing rs2 equality term should recover CoreMark cycles\\nwith much less timing risk than prior load bypasses, while preserving bus\\nbackpressure, replay, traps, RVFI ordering, and the nret=1 interface.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive a compact rs2-consumed qualifier for OP, STORE, and BRANCH opcodes and gate only the rs2 equality term of load-use detection, preserving all true dependencies and existing control priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the full current IF instruction or its opcode into hazard detection instead of only unconditional register-field tags, without changing the top-level interface or any pipeline handshake.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_hazard.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks proving true rs1 and rs2 load dependencies still bubble while accidental [24:20] matches in immediate, load, jump, upper-immed