{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat cores/bench/core.yaml && rg -n \\\"branch_target_buffer|core_pkg.sv\\\" formal/run_all.sh fpga/scripts test/cosim Makefile cores/bench -g '\"'!rtl/*'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 172.65\n  lut4: 10508\n  ff: 2026\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260711-003-r3s2\n  updated: '2026-07-11T13:47:15.122517Z'\nMakefile:99:\t    $(if $(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/core_pkg.sv),$(RTL_DIR)/core_pkg.sv) \\\nMakefile:100:\t    $(filter-out $(RTL_DIR)/core_pkg.sv,$(wildcard $(RTL_DIR)/*.sv)); \\\nformal/run_all.sh:139:# and rebuild from the glob, with core_pkg.sv first and wrapper.sv last.\nformal/run_all.sh:144:    [ -f \"$CORE_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && \\\nformal/run_all.sh:145:        echo \"@basedir@/cores/@core@/core_pkg.sv\"\nformal/run_all.sh:148:        [ \"$name\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:3:# $rtl_dir/*.sv is globbed dynamically (core_pkg.sv first for compilation-\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:20:# Ordering: read core_pkg.sv first so its typedefs/localparams are\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:22:read_verilog -sv \"$rtl_dir/core_pkg.sv\"\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:25:# case; we filter core_pkg.sv out to avoid double-include.\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:27:    if {[file tail $f] == \"core_pkg.sv\"} { continue }\ntest/cosim/build.sh:5:# RTL_DIR (default: rtl/) is globbed dynamically (with core_pkg.sv forced\ntest/cosim/build.sh:34:# Glob $RTL_DIR/*.sv. core_pkg.sv first; the rest in a stable lexicographic\ntest/cosim/build.sh:36:# about). If core_pkg.sv is missing the build will catch that downstream\ntest/cosim/build.sh:39:[ -f \"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && RTL_FILES+=(\"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\")\ntest/cosim/build.sh:41:  [ \"$(basename \"$f\")\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\ncores/bench/rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv:9:`include \"core_pkg.sv\"\ncores/bench/rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv:12:module branch_target_buffer (\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static backward-branch and direct-JAL predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Every taken branch, JAL, and JALR currently redirects only when it reaches EX,\\nflushing the younger fetch/decode work. CoreMark contains loop-closing backward\\nbranches and direct calls, so this repeated control penalty reduces iterations\\nper cycle. A decode-light static predictor can remove most of those bubbles\\nwithout a BHT, BTB, or return stack, which is important because the current core\\nis already close to its LUT target and fitness also depends on FPGA Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Every taken branch, JAL, and JALR currently redirects only when it reaches EX,\\nflushing the younger fetch/decode work. CoreMark contains loop-closing backward\\nbranches and direct calls, so this repeated control penalty reduces iterations\\nper cycle. A decode-light static predictor can remove most of those bubbles\\nwithout a BHT, BTB, or return stack, which is important because the current core\\nis already close to its LUT target and fitness also depends on FPGA Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Predict legal backward conditional branches taken and all word-aligned direct\\nJAL targets in IF, while predicting forward branches and JALR fall-through.\\nCarry the predicted next PC with the instruction to EX and redirect only when\\nthe resolved architectural next PC differs from that prediction. Correct loop\\nand direct-call predictions therefore avoid the existing two-younger-instruction\\nflush, while wrong predictions recover through the existing redirect path.\\n\\nKeep prediction combinational and stateless: recognize the B-type opcode plus\\nlegal funct3 and use the immediate sign bit for backward-taken, recognize JAL,\\nform each target directly from instruction bits, and require word alignment.\\nEX remains authoritative for branch conditions, JALR targets, misalignment\\ntraps, and RVFI pc_wdata. Redirect must retain priority over all bus stalls, and\\nprediction metadata must remain attached to a held instruction so random imem\\nand dmem backpressure cannot cause stale or duplicate execution.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with predicted-next-PC metadata so each instruction carries the exact fetch decision that EX must validate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-light BTFNT conditional-branch and direct-JAL prediction, advance the PC to aligned predicted targets, preserve redirect-over-stall priority, and emit the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX with the same stall and flush behavior as the instruction, PC, operands, and valid bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC against the carried prediction and assert redirect only on mismatch, while preserving JALR recovery and all existing misalignment-trap and RVFI pc_wdata semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat redirect as misprediction recovery rather than every taken control transfer, preserving the existing flush, load-use, and bus-backpressure priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for backward taken and not-taken branches, forward branches, direct JAL, JALR fallback, misaligned targets, and recovery coincident with imem or dmem stalls.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with predicted-next-PC metadata so each instruction carries the exact fetch decision that EX must validate.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-light BTFNT conditional-branch and direct-JAL prediction, advance the PC to aligned predicted targets, preserve redirect-over-stall priority, and emit the prediction metadata with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX with the same stall and flush behavior as the instruction, PC, operands, and valid bit.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC against the carried prediction and assert redirect only on mismatch, while preserving JALR recovery and all existing misalignment-trap and RVFI pc_wdata semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat redirect as misprediction recovery rather than every taken control transfer, preserving the existing flush, load-use, and bus-backpressure priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed checks for backward taken and not-taken branches, forward branches, direct JAL, JALR fallback, misaligned targets, and recovery coincident with imem or dmem stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 307.6, \"delta_pct\": 8.76, \"vs_baseline\": 8.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 131.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10330, \"ff\": 1895, \"seeds\": [114.32, 133.08, 131.03], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T12:58:54.342951Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.76%): Combinational IF opcode/immediate decode, parallel B/J target adders, and a 32-bit predicted-next-PC path can cost more FPGA Fmax than CoreMark recovers from avoided control bubbles, so prediction must stay off the fetch PC feedback cone.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"One-entry taken-target instruction replay buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Both earlier predictors reduced CoreMark cycles, but their target selection\\nlogic drove the fetch-address path and destroyed routed Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\nbackward loops repeatedly return to the same first instruction, so retaining\\nthat instruction can recover control-hazard cycles without predicting through\\nthe normal instruction-memory address cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Both earlier predictors reduced CoreMark cycles, but their target selection\\nlogic drove the fetch-address path and destroyed routed Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\nbackward loops repeatedly return to the same first instruction, so retaining\\nthat instruction can recover control-hazard cycles without predicting through\\nthe normal instruction-memory address cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry branch target instruction buffer specialized for a repeatedly\\ntaken backward conditional branch. On the first taken instance, use the\\nexisting EX redirect normally and capture the target instruction when that\\nredirected fetch is accepted. On a later taken instance of the same branch,\\nEX already knows the architectural outcome; replay the registered target\\ninstruction directly into ID/EX and redirect the registered fetch PC to the\\ncached target-plus-four address. This replaces the two wrong-path bubbles with\\nuseful target execution for the hottest loop while making no speculative\\nchange to io_imemAddr and adding no lookup to the sequential PC feedback path.\\n\\nThe entry holds branch-PC and target tags, the target instruction, and the\\ntarget-plus-four address. Fill, replay, and pending-fill state must advance\\nonly on accepted instruction fetches and must remain aligned across imem and\\ndmem stalls. Nonmatching branches, forward branches, jumps, illegal or\\nmisaligned controls, and not-taken outcomes retain the current behavior.\\nEX remains authoritative for direction, traps, RVFI pc_wdata, and recovery,\\nso this optimization cannot execute an unconfirmed target instruction.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact replay payload carrying the cached target instruction, its PC, and valid state into the ID/EX capture path without changing architectural pipeline or RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry backward-branch target instruction buffer with branch and target tags, accepted-fetch fill tracking, EX-confirmed hit detection, and stall-safe state updates.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the replay buffer, connect accepted fetch and resolved branch information, and select the cached target payload for ID/EX only on a confirmed taken hit while preserving the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the accepted fetch PC/instruction for target fill and, on an EX-confirmed replay hit, update the registered PC to cached target-plus-four through the existing redirect update point; keep io_imemAddr driven directly by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a replay input that atomically replaces the wrong-path decode payload with the cached target instruction on a confirmed hit, with reset, flush, load-use, and dmem-stall priorities preventing loss or duplication.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose legal resolved backward-branch PC, target, and taken status, and distinguish normal redirect from a replay hit while leaving architectural pc_next, trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate confirmed replay with redirect flushing so wrong-path fetch/decode state is killed but the injected target instruction is retained, including coincident bus and load-use stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for cold fill, repeated backward-taken replay, branch-tag mismatch, target replacement, not-taken behavior, and replay alignment under imem and dmem backpressure.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact replay payload carrying the cached target instruction, its PC, and valid state into the ID/EX capture path without changing architectural pipeline or RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_target_buffer.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a one-entry backward-branch target instruction buffer with branch and target tags, accepted-fetch fill tracking, EX-confirmed hit detection, and stall-safe state updates.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate the replay buffer, connect accepted fetch and resolved branch information, and select the cached target payload for ID/EX only on a confirmed taken hit while preserving the nret=1 interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the accepted fetch PC/instruction for target fill and, on an EX-confirmed replay hit, update the registered PC to cached target-plus-four through the existing redirect update point; keep io_imemAddr driven directly by the PC register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a replay input that atomically replaces the wrong-path decode payload with the cached target instruction on a confirmed hit, with reset, flush, load-use, and dmem-stall priorities preventing loss or duplication.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose legal resolved backward-branch PC, target, and taken status, and distinguish normal redirect from a replay hit while leaving architectural pc_next, trap, forwarding, and RVFI behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate confirmed replay with redirect flushing so wrong-path fetch/decode state is killed but the injected target instruction is retained, including coincident bus and load-use stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for cold fill, repeated backward-taken replay, branch-tag mismatch, target replacement, not-taken behavior, and replay alignment under imem and dmem backpressure.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 406.58, \"delta_pct\": 0.45, \"vs_baseline\": 43.76, \"fmax_mhz\": 172.65, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4246355, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10508, \"ff\": 2026, \"seeds\": [195.89, 168.04, 172.65], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T13:44:48.952189Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r3s2 (improvement, +0.45%): Replaying a cached target instruction only after EX confirms a repeated taken backward branch can recover CoreMark loop bubbles without putting target selection on io_imemAddr, though the small gain shows this narrow one-entry opportunity has limited coverage.\"}\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv:1:// rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:3:Constants mirror rtl/core_pkg.sv. If a localparam there changes, change\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:14:# ── ALU encodings (rtl/core_pkg.sv) ────────────────────────────────────────\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py:54:    package files (e.g. core_pkg.sv) come first.\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv:172:  branch_target_buffer u_btb (\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:371:            \"core_pkg.sv\",\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:376:            \"branch_target_buffer.sv\",\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py:334:               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"decoder.sv\"],\ncores/bench/test/test_predictor.py:135:        toplevel=\"branch_target_buffer\",\ncores/bench/test/test_predictor.py:136:        sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"branch_target_buffer.sv\"],\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:237:               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"alu.sv\"],\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
